    "global index": "AsDiv_1425",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A boat goes 30 km upstream and 44 km downstream in 10 hours. In 13 hours, it can go 40 km upstream and 55 km downstream.\n\nQuestion: Determine the speed of the stream and that of boat in still water.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the speed of the boat in still water be $b$ km/hr and the speed of the stream be $s$ km/hr.\nWhen the boat goes upstream, the effective speed is $(b-s)$ km/hr.\nWhen the boat goes downstream, the effective speed is $(b+s)$ km/hr.\n\nFrom the problem statement, we have two scenarios:\n\nScenario 1:\nA boat goes 30 km upstream and 44 km downstream in 10 hours.\nTime taken to go 30 km upstream = $\\frac{30}{b-s}$ hours\nTime taken to go 44 km downstream = $\\frac{44}{b+s}$ hours\nTotal time = $\\frac{30}{b-s} + \\frac{44}{b+s} = 10$ hours.  (Equation 1)\n\nScenario 2:\nIn 13 hours, it can go 40 km upstream and 55 km downstream.\nTime taken to go 40 km upstream = $\\frac{40}{b-s}$ hours\nTime taken to go 55 km downstream = $\\frac{55}{b+s}$ hours\nTotal time = $\\frac{40}{b-s} + \\frac{55}{b+s} = 13$ hours. (Equation 2)\n\nLet $x = \\frac{1}{b-s}$ and $y = \\frac{1}{b+s}$.\nNow the equations become:\n1) $30x + 44y = 10$\n2) $40x + 55y = 13$\n\nWe can solve this system of linear equations for $x$ and $y$.\nMultiply Equation 1 by 4 and Equation 2 by 3 to eliminate $x$:\n$4(30x + 44y) = 4(10) \\implies 120x + 176y = 40$\n$3(40x + 55y) = 3(13) \\implies 120x + 165y = 39$\n\nSubtract the second new equation from the first new equation:\n$(120x + 176y) - (120x + 165y) = 40 - 39$\n$11y = 1$\n$y = \\frac{1}{11}$\n\nSubstitute the value of $y$ into Equation 1:\n$30x + 44(\\frac{1}{11}) = 10$\n$30x + 4 = 10$\n$30x = 10 - 4$\n$30x = 6$\n$x = \\frac{6}{30} = \\frac{1}{5}$\n\nNow we have $x = \\frac{1}{b-s} = \\frac{1}{5}$ and $y = \\frac{1}{b+s} = \\frac{1}{11}$.\nFrom these, we get:\n$b-s = 5$ (Equation 3)\n$b+s = 11$ (Equation 4)\n\nAdd Equation 3 and Equation 4:\n$(b-s) + (b+s) = 5 + 11$\n$2b = 16$\n$b = 8$\n\nSubstitute the value of $b$ into Equation 4:\n$8 + s = 11$\n$s = 11 - 8$\n$s = 3$\n\nThe speed of the boat in still water is 8 km/hr, and the speed of the stream is 3 km/hr.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{{Speed \\ of \\ boat \\ in \\ still \\ water = 8 \\ km/hr, \\ Speed \\ of \\ stream = 3 \\ km/hr}}$.",
