    "global index": "AsDiv_1427",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A sailor goes 8 km downstream in 40 minutes and comes back in 1 hour.\n\nQuestion: Determine the speed of the sailor in still water and the speed of current.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $v_s$ be the speed of the sailor in still water and $v_c$ be the speed of the current.\nWhen sailing downstream, the effective speed is $v_s + v_c$.\nWhen sailing upstream, the effective speed is $v_s - v_c$.\n\nGiven that the sailor goes 8 km downstream in 40 minutes.\nTime = 40 minutes = 40/60 hours = 2/3 hours.\nDistance = 8 km.\nSpeed = Distance / Time\nSo, $v_s + v_c = 8 / (2/3) = 8 * (3/2) = 12$ km/hr.  (Equation 1)\n\nGiven that the sailor comes back in 1 hour.\nTime = 1 hour.\nDistance = 8 km.\nSo, $v_s - v_c = 8 / 1 = 8$ km/hr.  (Equation 2)\n\nNow we have a system of two linear equations:\n1) $v_s + v_c = 12$\n2) $v_s - v_c = 8$\n\nAdd Equation 1 and Equation 2:\n$(v_s + v_c) + (v_s - v_c) = 12 + 8$\n$2v_s = 20$\n$v_s = 20 / 2$\n$v_s = 10$ km/hr\n\nSubstitute the value of $v_s$ into Equation 1:\n$10 + v_c = 12$\n$v_c = 12 - 10$\n$v_c = 2$ km/hr\n\nThe speed of the sailor in still water is 10 km/hr and the speed of the current is 2 km/hr.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{{text{Sailor's speed: 10 km/hr, Current speed: 2 km/hr}}}$",
