  {
    "global index": "AsDiv_1348",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A field is in the shape of an equilateral triangle attached to the width of the rectangular region where width of the rectangle and side of the triangle measures the same. The length of rectangular region is 76 ft and the side of triangular region measures 42 ft.\n\nQuestion: Find the perimeter of the field.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The field consists of a rectangle and an equilateral triangle attached to one of its sides.\nThe length of the rectangle is 76 ft.\nThe width of the rectangle is equal to the side of the equilateral triangle, which is 42 ft.\n\nTo find the perimeter of the field, we need to add the lengths of all the outer boundaries. The perimeter will consist of the length of the rectangle, the two sides of the rectangle that are not attached to the triangle, and the two sides of the equilateral triangle that are not attached to the rectangle.\n\nThe length of the rectangle is 76 ft.\nThe width of the rectangle is 42 ft.\nThe side of the equilateral triangle is 42 ft.\n\nThe perimeter of the field is the sum of the length of the rectangle, the width of the rectangle that is not part of the triangle's attachment, and the two remaining sides of the equilateral triangle.\nPerimeter = Length of rectangle + Width of rectangle + Side of triangle + Side of triangle\nPerimeter = 76 ft + 42 ft + 42 ft + 42 ft\n\nHowever, the problem states that the equilateral triangle is *attached to the width* of the rectangular region. This means one side of the rectangle, which has a length equal to the width (42 ft), is shared with one side of the equilateral triangle.\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of the field will be the length of the rectangle, the other width of the rectangle, and the two exposed sides of the equilateral triangle.\n\nPerimeter = Length of rectangle + Width of rectangle (not attached to triangle) + Side of triangle (not attached to rectangle) + Side of triangle (not attached to rectangle)\n\nAlternatively, we can think of it as:\nPerimeter = (2 * Length of rectangle) + (2 * Width of rectangle) - (side shared with triangle) + (2 * Sides of triangle) - (side shared with rectangle)\nSince one width of the rectangle is shared with one side of the triangle, these two sides cancel out in the perimeter calculation.\n\nPerimeter = Length of rectangle + Width of rectangle + Side of triangle + Side of triangle\nPerimeter = 76 ft + 42 ft + 42 ft + 42 ft\n\nLet's re-read the problem statement carefully: \"A field is in the shape of an equilateral triangle attached to the width of the rectangular region where width of the rectangle and side of the triangle measures the same.\"\n\nThis means one of the 42 ft sides of the rectangle is where the triangle is attached.\nSo, the perimeter will be the length of the rectangle, the other width of the rectangle, and the two other sides of the triangle.\n\nPerimeter = Length of rectangle + Width of rectangle (opposite to the attached side) + Side of triangle + Side of triangle\nPerimeter = 76 ft + 42 ft + 42 ft + 42 ft\n\nPerimeter = 76 + 42 + 42 + 42\nPerimeter = 76 + (3 * 42)\nPerimeter = 76 + 126\nPerimeter = 202 ft\n\nThe perimeter of the field is the sum of the length of the rectangle, the width of the rectangle not attached to the triangle, and the two exposed sides of the equilateral triangle. We are given the length of the rectangle as 76 ft and the side of the equilateral triangle as 42 ft, which is also the width of the rectangle.\nThe perimeter is calculated as 76 ft (length) + 42 ft (width) + 42 ft (triangle side) + 42 ft (triangle side).\n\nPerimeter = 76 + 42 + 42 + 42\nPerimeter = 76 + 126\nPerimeter = 202\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{202}$.",
