      "generated_answer": "First, convert all time intervals to minutes. Carpenter A takes 40 minutes per door. Carpenter B takes 1 hour and 20 minutes, which is $60 + 20 = 80$ minutes per door. Carpenter C takes 1 hour and 40 minutes, which is $60 + 40 = 100$ minutes per door.\n\nNext, find the least common multiple (LCM) of 40, 80, and 100 to determine when they will finish installing doors simultaneously. The LCM of 40, 80, and 100 is 400 minutes.\n\nFinally, add 400 minutes to the starting time of 9:15. 400 minutes is equal to 6 hours and 40 minutes ($400 \\div 60 = 6$ with a remainder of $40$). Adding 6 hours and 40 minutes to 9:15 gives us 3:55 PM.\n\nThe carpenters will install doors at the same time again after 400 minutes.\n400 minutes = 6 hours and 40 minutes.\nStarting time: 9:15 AM\nAdding 6 hours to 9:15 AM gives 3:15 PM.\nAdding 40 minutes to 3:15 PM gives 3:55 PM.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{{3:55 PM}}$.",
