    "global index": "AsDiv_1428",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: Points A and B are 70 km apart on a highway. A car starts from A and another car starts from B at the same time. If they travel in the same direction, they meet in 7 hours, but if they travel towards each other they meet in one hour.\n\nQuestion: What are their respective speeds?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $v_A$ be the speed of the car starting from A and $v_B$ be the speed of the car starting from B. The distance between A and B is 70 km.\n\nCase 1: They travel in the same direction.\nIf they travel in the same direction, assume the car from A is faster than the car from B, so it catches up to B. The relative speed is $v_A - v_B$. They meet in 7 hours.\nDistance = Speed × Time\n$70 = (v_A - v_B) \\times 7$\n$v_A - v_B = \\frac{70}{7}$\n$v_A - v_B = 10$ (Equation 1)\n\nCase 2: They travel towards each other.\nIf they travel towards each other, their relative speed is $v_A + v_B$. They meet in 1 hour.\nDistance = Speed × Time\n$70 = (v_A + v_B) \\times 1$\n$v_A + v_B = 70$ (Equation 2)\n\nNow we have a system of two linear equations with two variables:\n1) $v_A - v_B = 10$\n2) $v_A + v_B = 70$\n\nAdd Equation 1 and Equation 2:\n$(v_A - v_B) + (v_A + v_B) = 10 + 70$\n$2v_A = 80$\n$v_A = \\frac{80}{2}$\n$v_A = 40$ km/h\n\nSubstitute the value of $v_A$ into Equation 2:\n$40 + v_B = 70$\n$v_B = 70 - 40$\n$v_B = 30$ km/h\n\nThus, the speed of the car from A is 40 km/h and the speed of the car from B is 30 km/h.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{{v_A = 40, v_B = 30}}$.",
