    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The passage describes a country where almost all the population shares the same ethnicity (Danes), religion (Lutheran), and language (Danish). This homogeneity, where the state and the nation largely overlap, is the defining characteristic of a nation-state.\n\nA city-state is a sovereign state that consists of a city and its dependent territories. A microstate is an extremely small sovereign state. A stateless nation is an ethnic group or nation that does not possess its own state. A political boundary is simply a line that marks the limits of an area. Therefore, Denmark, as described, exemplifies a nation-state.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
