    "global index": "GeoBench_1341",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following illustrates the multiplier effect?\n\nOptions: \nA. The steel industry has historically been the main focus of Pittsburgh’s economy.\nB. The steel industry in Pittsburgh has led to the expansion of the area’s construction industries which has led to the expansion of raw material supply companies.\nC. New restaurants have opened in Pittsburgh to help feed the community of steel workers.\nD. The features of Pittsburgh’s location make it an ideal spot to manufacture steel.\nE. Pittsburgh’s access to raw materials, clean water, and varied energy sources allows workers to propel the steel industry.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The multiplier effect in economics describes how an initial change in spending can lead to a larger overall change in the economy. Option B illustrates this by showing a chain reaction of economic growth: the steel industry leads to growth in construction, which in turn leads to growth in raw material supply. This demonstrates how an initial increase in activity in one sector can have cascading positive effects on related sectors. Options A, C, D, and E describe factors related to the steel industry's presence or features in Pittsburgh but do not illustrate the interconnected and expanding nature of spending and economic activity characteristic of the multiplier effect.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
      "success": true,
