    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to the rank-size rule, in a country whose largest city contains 800,000 people, its fourth-largest city contains\n\nOptions: \nA. 1,600,000 people\nB. 800,000 people\nC. 400,000 people\nD. 200,000 people\nE. 100,000 people\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The rank-size rule states that the population of a city is inversely proportional to its rank. This means that if the largest city has a population P, the second-largest city will have a population of P/2, the third-largest city will have P/3, and so on. Therefore, the fourth-largest city will have a population of P/4.\n\nGiven that the largest city contains 800,000 people, the fourth-largest city would contain 800,000 / 4 = 200,000 people.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
