    "global index": "GeoBench_999",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The largest city in \"Country X\" has 18 million people. According to the rank-size rule, how many people will the third largest city in \"Country X\" have?\n\nOptions: \nA. 15 million\nB. 13 million\nC. 6 million\nD. 9 million\nE. 3 million\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The rank-size rule states that if a country's cities are ranked by population, the population of a city is inversely proportional to its rank. In other words, the second largest city will have approximately half the population of the largest city, the third largest city will have approximately one-third the population, and so on.\n\nGiven that the largest city has 18 million people, the third largest city would have approximately 18 million / 3 = 6 million people.\n\nTherefore, the most likely correct answer is **C**.\n\nThe rank-size rule suggests that the population of the nth largest city is approximately P/n, where P is the population of the largest city. In this case, P = 18 million and n = 3. So, the population of the third largest city would be approximately 18 million / 3 = 6 million people.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 132,
        "output_tokens": 193,
        "total_tokens": 325
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": null,
    "accuracy": null
  },
