compute $z_2 = F(z_1) = F(1+274i) = \\frac{1+274i+i}{1+274i-i} = \\frac{1+275i}{1+273i}$.\n\nConsider $z_n+i$. $z_n+i = \\frac{z_{n-1}+i}{z_{n-1}-i}+i = \\frac{z_{n-1}+i+i(z_{n-1}-i)}{z_{n-1}-i} = \\frac{z_{n-1}+i+iz_{n-1}+1}{z_{n-1}-i}$.\nConsider $z_n-i$. $z_n-i = \\frac{z_{n-1}+i}{z_{n-1}-i}-i = \\frac{z_{n-1}+i-i(z_{n-1}-i)}{z_{n-1}-i} = \\frac{z_{n-1}+i-iz_{n-1}-1}{z_{n-1}-i}$.\n$\\frac{z_n+i}{z_n-i} = \\frac{z_{n-1}+i+iz_{n-1}+1}{z_{n-1}+i-iz_{n-1}-1} = \\frac{(1+i)z_{n-1}+1+i}{(1-i)z_{n-1}+i-1}$.\nLet $w_n = \\frac{z_n+i}{z_n-i}$. Then $w_n = \\frac{(1+i)z_{n-1}+1+i}{(1-i)z_{n-1}+i-1}$. This is not a simple recurrence relation for $w_n$.\n\nLet's try to compute $F(F(F(F(z))))$.\n$F(z) = \\frac{z+i}{z-i}$.\n$F^2(z) = \\frac{(1+i)(z+1)}{(1-i)(z-1)}$.\n$F^3(z) = F(F^2(z)) = \\frac{\\frac{(1+i)(z+1)}{(1-i)(z-1)}+i}{\\frac{(1+i)(z+1)}{(1-i)(z-1)}-i} = \\frac{(1+i)(z+1)+i(1-i)(z-1)}{(1+i)(z+1)-i(1-i)(z-1)} = \\frac{(1+i)(z+1)+(1+i)(z-1)}{(1+i)(z+1)-(1+i)(z-1)} = \\frac{(1+i)(z+1+z-1)}{(1+i)(z+1-(z-1))} = \\frac{2z}{2} = z$.\nSo $F^3(z) = z$.\nTherefore, the sequence is periodic with period 3: $z_0, z_1, z_2, z_0, z_1, z_2, \\ldots$.\nWe want to find $z_{2002}$.\nSince the period is 3, we need to find the remainder of 2002 when divided by 3.\n$2002 = 3 \\times 667 + 1$.\nSo $z_{2002} = z_1$.\n$z_1 = F(z_0) = F(\\frac{1}{137}+i) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137}+i+i}{\\frac{1}{137}+i-i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137}+2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 2i \\cdot 137 = 1+274i$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{1+274i}$.",
