      "generated_answer": "When the point $(0,0)$ is reflected over the vertical line $x=1$, the x-coordinate changes while the y-coordinate remains the same. The distance from $(0,0)$ to $x=1$ is $1-0=1$. So, the reflected point will be $1+1=2$ units to the right of the line $x=1$, making the new x-coordinate $1+1=2$. The reflected point is $(2,0)$.\n\nNext, when the point $(2,0)$ is reflected over the horizontal line $y=2$, the y-coordinate changes while the x-coordinate remains the same. The distance from $(2,0)$ to $y=2$ is $2-0=2$. So, the reflected point will be $2+2=4$ units above the line $y=2$, making the new y-coordinate $2+2=4$. The resulting point is $(2,4)$.\n\nThe final answer is \\boxed{{(2, 4)}}.",
