    "global index": "MATH_492",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem and provide the final answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The set of vectors $\\mathbf{{v}}$ such that\n\\[\\operatorname{{proj}}_{{\\begin{{pmatrix}} 2 \\\\ 1 \\end{{pmatrix}} \\mathbf{{v}} = \\begin{{pmatrix}} 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{{pmatrix}}\\]lie on a line.  Enter the equation of this line in the form \"$y = mx + b$\".\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $\\mathbf{w} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix}$. The projection of $\\mathbf{v}$ onto $\\mathbf{w}$ is given by\n\\[\\operatorname{{proj}}_{\\mathbf{w}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w}}{\\|\\mathbf{w}\\|^2} \\mathbf{w}.\\]\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{{proj}}_{\\mathbf{w}} \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}$. This implies that\n\\[\\frac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w}}{\\|\\mathbf{w}\\|^2} \\mathbf{w} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\nSince $\\mathbf{w} \\neq \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}$, we must have $\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w} = 0$.\nThe dot product is $\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w} = \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} = 2x + y$.\nSetting the dot product to zero, we get $2x + y = 0$.\nThis equation can be rewritten as $y = -2x$. This is the equation of a line passing through the origin.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{y = -2x}$.",
