    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A frameshift mutation is created when\n\nOptions: \nA. a base pair is moved from one location in a gene to another\nB. a codon's nucleotide sequence changes so that it calls for production of a different amino acid than the original one\nC. telomeric sequences are removed from DNA\nD. a base pair is either inserted or deleted in a gene\nE. a large portion of a chromosome is deleted\nF. a gene is duplicated within the DNA sequence\nG. a codon's nucleotide sequence is changed so that it no longer codes for any amino acid\nH. a base pair is replaced with a different base pair in a gene\nI. a codon's nucleotide sequence is changed so that it codes for the same amino acid\nJ. a codon's nucleotide sequence is changed so that instead of coding for a given amino acid it acts to terminate translation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
