      "generated_answer": "**Explanation:**\n\nA standard deck has 52 cards. There are 12 face cards (Jack, Queen, King of each suit). There are 4 aces.\n\n*   The probability of drawing a face card on the first draw is 12/52.\n*   After drawing a face card, there are 51 cards left. The probability of drawing an ace on the second draw is 4/51.\n\nThe combined probability is (12/52) * (4/51) = 48 / 2652. Simplifying this fraction gives 4/221.\n\n**Answer:** The probability that a face card is drawn on the first draw and an ace on the second in two consecutive draws, without replacement, from a standard deck of cards is 4/221.\n\nThe correct option is **J**.",
