      "generated_answer": "The probability of getting a 5 on a single roll of a balanced die is 1/6. Since the two rolls are independent events, the probability of getting a 5 on each of two successive rolls is the product of the individual probabilities. Therefore, the probability is (1/6) * (1/6) = 1/36.\n\nThe correct answer is E.\n\nFinal Answer: \\boxed{E}",
