      "generated_answer": "To find the Z-score, we use the formula: $Z = (X - \\mu) / \\sigma$, where $X$ is the raw score, $\\mu$ is the mean, and $\\sigma$ is the standard deviation.\n\nFor a raw score of 115:\n$Z = (115 - 118) / 11 = -3 / 11 \\approx -0.27$\n\nFor a raw score of 134:\n$Z = (134 - 118) / 11 = 16 / 11 \\approx 1.45$\n\nFor a raw score of 99:\n$Z = (99 - 118) / 11 = -19 / 11 \\approx -1.73$\n\nTherefore, the Z-scores are approximately -0.27, 1.45, and -1.73.\n\nComparing these values to the given options, option F matches these calculated Z-scores.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{F}$.",
