    "global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3279",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If X has a normal distribution with mean 9 and standard deviation 3, find P(5 < X < 11).\n\nOptions: \nA. - .09176\nB. .21185\nC. .37748\nD. .55962\nE. .65361\nF. .09176\nG. .92715\nH. .47568\nI. .81743\nJ. .74537\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find $P(5 < X < 11)$ for a normal distribution with mean $\\mu = 9$ and standard deviation $\\sigma = 3$, we need to convert the X values to z-scores. The formula for a z-score is $z = (X - \\mu) / \\sigma$.\n\nFor $X = 5$, the z-score is $z_1 = (5 - 9) / 3 = -4 / 3 \\approx -1.333$.\nFor $X = 11$, the z-score is $z_2 = (11 - 9) / 3 = 2 / 3 \\approx 0.667$.\n\nNow we need to find $P(-1.333 < Z < 0.667)$, where Z is a standard normal variable. This can be calculated as $P(Z < 0.667) - P(Z < -1.333)$.\nUsing a standard normal distribution table or calculator, we find:\n$P(Z < 0.667) \\approx 0.7475$\n$P(Z < -1.333) \\approx 0.09176$\n\nTherefore, $P(5 < X < 11) = P(Z < 0.667) - P(Z < -1.333) \\approx 0.7475 - 0.09176 = 0.65574$.\n\nLet's recheck the z-scores and corresponding probabilities more precisely.\n$z_1 = (5 - 9) / 3 = -4/3 \\approx -1.3333$\n$z_2 = (11 - 9) / 3 = 2/3 \\approx 0.6667$\n\nUsing a z-table or calculator:\n$P(Z < 0.6667) \\approx 0.74751$\n$P(Z < -1.3333) \\approx 0.09176$\n\n$P(5 < X < 11) = P(Z < 2/3) - P(Z < -4/3) \\approx 0.74751 - 0.09176 = 0.65575$.\n\nLooking at the options, option E, 0.65361, is the closest.\n\nLet's calculate with higher precision to confirm.\nUsing a calculator:\n$P(Z < 2/3) \\approx 0.747507$\n$P(Z < -4/3) \\approx 0.091759$\n$P(5 < X < 11) = 0.747507 - 0.091759 = 0.655748$.\n\nThe closest option is E. 0.65361. There might be slight rounding differences in the provided options or they are based on a less precise z-table.\n\nLet's verify other options to see if there's a pattern.\n\nConsider the options.\nOption F is 0.09176, which is $P(Z < -4/3)$. This is part of the calculation but not the final answer.\nIf we consider $P(-1.33 < X < 1.33)$, where X are z-scores:\n$z_1 = -1.33 \\implies P = 0.0918$\n$z_2 = 1.33 \\implies P = 0.9082$\n$0.9082 - 0.0918 = 0.8164$, which is close to option I.\n\nLet's check if any of the options correspond to other simple error calculations.\n\nGiven the provided options, the closest answer to our calculated value of approximately 0.65575 is 0.65361. This suggests that there might be minor rounding differences or the question might intend for a less precise approximation.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
