    "global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3107",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given a mean of 50 and a standard deviation of 10 for a set of measurements that is normally distributed, find the probability that a randomly selected observation is between 50 and 55.\n\nOptions: \nA. .125\nB. .341\nC. .180\nD. .210\nE. .274\nF. .159\nG. .300\nH. .191\nI. .200\nJ. .230\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability that a randomly selected observation is between 50 and 55, we need to calculate the z-score for 55. The formula for the z-score is $z = (x - \\mu) / \\sigma$, where x is the observation, $\\mu$ is the mean, and $\\sigma$ is the standard deviation. In this case, $z = (55 - 50) / 10 = 5 / 10 = 0.5$. We then need to find the area under the standard normal curve between $z=0$ (which corresponds to the mean) and $z=0.5$. Looking up the z-score of 0.5 in a standard normal distribution table, we find the probability to be approximately 0.1915.\n\nComparing this probability to the given options, option H, 0.191, is the closest value.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{H}$.",
