  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3049",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Miniature poodles are thought to have a mean height of 12 inches and a standard deviation of 1.8 inches. If height is measured to the nearest inch, find the percentage of poodles having a height exceeding 14 inches.\n\nOptions: \nA. 45 percent\nB. 2.5 percent\nC. 5 percent\nD. 30 percent\nE. 20 percent\nF. 10 percent\nG. 15 percent\nH. 35 percent\nI. 40 percent\nJ. 25 percent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we can use the concept of the normal distribution. The mean height is $\\mu = 12$ inches and the standard deviation is $\\sigma = 1.8$ inches. We want to find the percentage of poodles with a height exceeding 14 inches. Since height is measured to the nearest inch, we consider the continuous range from 13.5 inches upwards.\n\nFirst, we calculate the z-score for a height of 13.5 inches:\n$z = (x - \\mu) / \\sigma = (13.5 - 12) / 1.8 = 1.5 / 1.8 = 5/6 \\approx 0.8333$\n\nNow, we look up the area to the left of this z-score in a standard normal distribution table or use a calculator. The area to the left of $z = 0.8333$ is approximately 0.7977.\nSince we want the percentage of poodles having a height exceeding 14 inches (which corresponds to heights greater than or equal to 13.5 inches), we need to find the area to the right of $z = 0.8333$.\nArea to the right = $1$ - Area to the left = $1 - 0.7977 = 0.2023$\n\nConverting this to a percentage, we get $0.2023 \\times 100\\% = 20.23\\%$.\n\nComparing this result with the given options, 20 percent is the closest value.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 182,
        "output_tokens": 360,
        "total_tokens": 542
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
