    "global index": "MMLUPro_biology_3322",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An actress with O type blood accused a producer with B type blood of being the father of her child in a paternity suit. The child was also O type. What does the blood type suggest about his guilt?\n\nOptions: \nA. He cannot be the father\nB. The child's blood type suggests the mother has been unfaithful\nC. The child's blood type suggests a mutation occurred\nD. He could have been the father but it does not prove it\nE. The blood type proves he is the father because O type is recessive\nF. He definitely is the father\nG. He must have been the father because B type blood can produce O type offspring\nH. The blood type does not suggest anything\nI. The child's O type blood proves his innocence\nJ. He is probably not the father because B type blood cannot produce O type offspring\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let's analyze the blood types.\nThe mother has O type blood. Her genotype for blood type is OO.\nThe father has B type blood. His genotype can be either BB or BO.\nThe child has O type blood. Their genotype is OO.\n\nFor the child to have OO blood type, they must inherit an O allele from each parent. The mother can only pass on an O allele. Therefore, the father must also be able to pass on an O allele. This means the father's genotype must be BO.\n\nIf the father's genotype is BO, he has B type blood (because B is dominant over O) and can indeed have an offspring with O type blood (if the child inherits the O allele from him and the O allele from the mother).\n\nTherefore, the blood type is consistent with the producer being the father. It does not definitively prove he is the father, as other men with BO genotype could also father an O type child with an O type mother. However, it certainly does not exclude him from being the father.\n\nThe most appropriate answer is that he could have been the father, but it does not prove it.\n\nOption A is incorrect because B type blood can produce O type offspring if the genotype is BO.\nOption B is incorrect, blood types do not suggest infidelity.\nOption C is incorrect, there's no indication of a mutation.\nOption D is correct.\nOption E is incorrect because while O is recessive, the statement does not prove he is the father.\nOption F is incorrect, it does not definitively prove he is the father.\nOption G is incorrect, while B type blood (genotype BO) can produce O type offspring, this doesn't mean he *must* have been the father.\nOption H is incorrect, the blood type does suggest he *could* be the father.\nOption I is incorrect, the child's blood type does not prove his innocence.\nOption J is incorrect because B type blood can produce O type offspring if the genotype is BO.\n\nThe correct answer is D.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
