      "generated_answer": "The question asks about the angular momentum of protons and neutrons. Protons and neutrons are composite particles made of quarks. Quarks have both spin and orbital angular momentum. Since protons and neutrons are made of quarks, they also possess both spin and orbital angular momentum. Spin angular momentum is an intrinsic property of the constituent quarks, while orbital angular momentum arises from the motion of the quarks within the nucleon.\n\nTherefore, both protons and neutrons possess both orbital and spin angular momentum.\n\nThe correct answer is **D**.",
