    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3462",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Evaluate the series\n$$\nS=\\sum_{{n=0}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{1}}{{3^n}}\n$$\n\nOptions: \nA. 2 / 3\nB. 1 / 2\nC. 1 / 3\nD. 3\nE. 7 / 4\nF. 4 / 3\nG. 5 / 3\nH. 2\nI. 5 / 2\nJ.  3 / 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given series is a geometric series with the first term $a = \\frac{1}{3^0} = 1$ and the common ratio $r = \\frac{1}{3}$. Since $|r| < 1$, the series converges to the sum $S = \\frac{a}{1-r}$. Substituting the values $a=1$ and $r=\\frac{1}{3}$, we get $S = \\frac{1}{1-\\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{2}{3}} = \\frac{3}{2}$.\n\nThe sum of the series is $\\frac{3}{2}$.\n\nComparing this value with the given options:\nA. 2 / 3\nB. 1 / 2\nC. 1 / 3\nD. 3\nE. 7 / 4\nF. 4 / 3\nG. 5 / 3\nH. 2\nI. 5 / 2\nJ. 3 / 2\n\nThe calculated sum matches option J.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{J}$.",
