    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3903",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $w$ be the variable defined as the number of heads that show when two coins are tossed simultaneously. Find $\\langle w\\rangle$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.25\nB.  1\nC. 3\nD. 0\nE. 2.5\nF. 2\nG. 1.25\nH. 1.5\nI. 0.75\nJ. 0.5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $w$ be the number of heads when two coins are tossed simultaneously. The possible values for $w$ are 0 (no heads), 1 (one head), and 2 (two heads). We can list the possible outcomes: HH, HT, TH, TT.\nThe probability of getting 0 heads (TT) is $\\frac{1}{4}$.\nThe probability of getting 1 head (HT or TH) is $\\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{1}{2}$.\nThe probability of getting 2 heads (HH) is $\\frac{1}{4}$.\nThe expected value $\\langle w\\rangle$ is calculated as:\n$\\langle w\\rangle = (0 \\times P(w=0)) + (1 \\times P(w=1)) + (2 \\times P(w=2))$\n$\\langle w\\rangle = (0 \\times \\frac{1}{4}) + (1 \\times \\frac{1}{2}) + (2 \\times \\frac{1}{4})$\n$\\langle w\\rangle = 0 + \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{2}{4}$\n$\\langle w\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}$\n$\\langle w\\rangle = 1$\n\nThe correct answer is B.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
