    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Solve 6x^2 - 7x - 20 = 0.\n\nOptions: \nA. 5/2, 4/3\nB. -5/3, 4/2\nC. 5/3, -4/2\nD. 2, -10\nE. 4, -5\nF. -5/2, 4/3\nG. -5/6, 4/5\nH. 5/2, -4/3\nI. 5, 4\nJ. 5, -4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve the quadratic equation $6x^2 - 7x - 20 = 0$, we can use the quadratic formula $x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}$. In this equation, $a=6$, $b=-7$, and $c=-20$.\n\nPlugging these values into the quadratic formula:\n$x = \\frac{-(-7) \\pm \\sqrt{(-7)^2 - 4(6)(-20)}}{2(6)}$\n$x = \\frac{7 \\pm \\sqrt{49 + 480}}{12}$\n$x = \\frac{7 \\pm \\sqrt{529}}{12}$\n$x = \\frac{7 \\pm 23}{12}$\n\nSo, the two solutions are:\n$x_1 = \\frac{7 + 23}{12} = \\frac{30}{12} = \\frac{5}{2}$\n$x_2 = \\frac{7 - 23}{12} = \\frac{-16}{12} = -\\frac{4}{3}$\n\nComparing these solutions to the given options, we find that option H has the values $5/2$ and $-4/3$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{H}$.",
