      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Grignard reagents are highly reactive and will react with water, leading to their decomposition into hydrocarbons, which will inactivate the reagent and prevent the desired reaction from occurring. Therefore, it is crucial to ensure that both the Grignard reagent and the aldehyde are free from moisture.",
