  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3622",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nitrous acid, HNO2, has a pKa value of 3.3. If a solution of nitrous acid is found to have a pH of 4.2, what can be said about the concentration of the conjugate acid/base pair found in solution?\n\nOptions: \nA. [HNO2] > [NO2-]\nB. [H2NO2+] < [NO2-]\nC. [NO2-] < [H2NO2+]\nD. [H2NO2+] > [NO2-]\nE. [NO2-] > [HNO2]\nF. [NO2-] = [HNO2]\nG. [H2NO2+] > [HNO2]\nH. [HNO2] = [H2NO2+]\nI. [HNO2] > [H2NO2+]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Henderson-Hasselbalch equation relates pH, pKa, and the concentrations of a weak acid and its conjugate base: pH = pKa + log([conjugate base]/[weak acid]). In this case, the weak acid is HNO2 and its conjugate base is NO2-. The equation becomes: 4.2 = 3.3 + log([NO2-]/[HNO2]). Solving for the ratio, we get log([NO2-]/[HNO2]) = 4.2 - 3.3 = 0.9. Therefore, [NO2-]/[HNO2] = 10^0.9 ≈ 7.94. This means that the concentration of the conjugate base (NO2-) is significantly greater than the concentration of the weak acid (HNO2).\n\nLet's examine the options:\nOption A: [HNO2] > [NO2-] is incorrect because [NO2-] > [HNO2].\nOption B: [H2NO2+] < [NO2-] involves the protonated form of nitrous acid, which is not the species involved in the acid-base equilibrium of nitrous acid in aqueous solution.\nOption C: [NO2-] < [H2NO2+] is incorrect for the same reason as option B.\nOption D: [H2NO2+] < [NO2-] is incorrect for the same reason as option B.\nOption E: [NO2-] > [HNO2] is correct because [NO2-]/[HNO2] is approximately 7.94.\nOption F: [NO2-] = [HNO2] is incorrect because the ratio is not 1.\nOption G: [H2NO2+] > [HNO2] is incorrect for the same reason as option B.\nOption H: [HNO2] = [H2NO2+] is incorrect for the same reason as option B.\nOption I: [HNO2] > [H2NO2+] is incorrect for the same reason as option B.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
      "success": true,
