  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4070",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The vibrational wavenumber of $\\mathrm{{Br}}_2$ is $323.2 \\mathrm{{~cm}}^{{-1}}$. Evaluate the vibrational partition function explicitly (without approximation) and plot its value as a function of temperature. At what temperature is the value within 5 per cent of the value calculated from the approximate formula?\n\nOptions: \nA. 7000 K\nB. 2500 K\nC. 3500$\\mathrm{{~K}}$\nD. 6000 K\nE. 2000 K\nF.  4500$\\mathrm{{~K}}$\nG. 4000$\\mathrm{{~K}}$\nH. 5500 K\nI. 5000$\\mathrm{{~K}}$\nJ. 3000 K\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The vibrational partition function for a diatomic molecule is given by:\n$q_{vib} = \\frac{1}{1 - e^{-\\Theta_v/T}}$\nwhere $\\Theta_v = \\frac{h\\nu}{k_B}$ is the characteristic vibrational temperature and $\\nu$ is the vibrational frequency. The vibrational wavenumber is given as $\\tilde{\\nu} = 323.2 \\mathrm{~cm}^{-1}$.\n\nFirst, we need to convert the wavenumber to frequency and then to the characteristic temperature:\n$\\nu = c \\tilde{\\nu}$\n$\\Theta_v = \\frac{hc\\tilde{\\nu}}{k_B}$\n\nGiven values:\n$c = 2.9979 \\times 10^{10} \\mathrm{~cm/s}$\n$h = 6.6261 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{~J \\cdot s}$\n$k_B = 1.3806 \\times 10^{-23} \\mathrm{~J/K}$\n$\\tilde{\\nu} = 323.2 \\mathrm{~cm}^{-1}$\n\nCalculate $\\Theta_v$:\n$\\Theta_v = \\frac{(6.6261 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{~J \\cdot s}) \\times (2.9979 \\times 10^{10} \\mathrm{~cm/s}) \\times (323.2 \\mathrm{~cm}^{-1})}{1.3806 \\times 10^{-23} \\mathrm{~J/K}}$\n$\\Theta_v \\approx 466.5 \\mathrm{~K}$\n\nThe approximate formula for the vibrational partition function at high temperatures is $q_{vib, \\text{approx}} \\approx \\frac{T}{\\Theta_v}$.\nWe are looking for the temperature at which the explicit calculation of $q_{vib}$ is within 5 per cent of the approximate value. This means:\n$|q_{vib} - q_{vib, \\text{approx}}| \\le 0.05 \\times q_{vib, \\text{approx}}$\n\nLet's express this condition in terms of $T$ and $\\Theta_v$:\n$|\\frac{1}{1 - e^{-\\Theta_v/T}} - \\frac{T}{\\Theta_v}| \\le 0.05 \\times \\frac{T}{\\Theta_v}$\n\nWe can check the given options for temperature.\n\nLet's test a few temperatures:\nIf $T = 2000 \\mathrm{~K}$:\n$\\Theta_v/T = 466.5 / 2000 = 0.23325$\n$e^{-\\Theta_v/T} = e^{-0.23325} \\approx 0.7925$\n$q_{vib} = \\frac{1}{1 - 0.7925} = \\frac{1}{0.2075} \\approx 4.819$\n$q_{vib, \\text{approx}} = \\frac{2000}{466.5} \\approx 4.287$\nDifference = $|4.819 - 4.287| = 0.532$\nPercentage difference = $(0.532 / 4.287) \\times 100\\% \\approx 12.4\\%$\n\nIf $T = 2500 \\mathrm{~K}$:\n$\\Theta_v/T = 466.5 / 2500 = 0.1866$\n$e^{-\\Theta_v/T} = e^{-0.1866} \\approx 0.8307$\n$q_{vib} = \\frac{1}{1 - 0.8307} = \\frac{1}{0.1693} \\approx 5.906$\n$q_{vib, \\text{approx}} = \\frac{2500}{466.5} \\approx 5.360$\nDifference = $|5.906 - 5.360| = 0.546$\nPercentage difference = $(0.546 / 5.360) \\times 100\\% \\approx 10.2\\%$\n\nIf $T = 3000 \\mathrm{~K}$:\n$\\Theta_v/T = 466.5 / 3000 = 0.1555$\n$e^{-\\Theta_v/T} = e^{-0.1555} \\approx 0.8561$\n$q_{vib} = \\frac{1}{1 - 0.8561} = \\frac{1}{0.1439} \\approx 6.950$\n$q_{vib, \\text{approx}} = \\frac{3000}{466.5} \\approx 6.431$\nDifference = $|6.950 - 6.431| = 0.519$\nPercentage difference = $(0.519 / 6.431) \\times 100\\% \\approx 8.07\\%$\n\nIf $T = 3500 \\mathrm{~K}$:\n$\\Theta_v/T = 466.5 / 3500 = 0.1333$\n$e^{-\\Theta_v/T} = e^{-0.1333} \\approx 0.8754$\n$q_{vib} = \\frac{1}{1 - 0.8754} = \\frac{1}{0.1246} \\approx 8.026$\n$q_{vib, \\text{approx}} = \\frac{3500}{466.5} \\approx 7.502$\nDifference = $|8.026 - 7.502| = 0.524$\nPercentage difference = $(0.524 / 7.502) \\times 100\\% \\approx 6.99\\%$\n\nIf $T = 4000 \\mathrm{~K}$:\n$\\Theta_v/T = 466.5 / 4000 = 0.1166$\n$e^{-\\Theta_v/T} = e^{-0.1166} \\approx 0.8899$\n$q_{vib} = \\frac{1}{1 - 0.8899} = \\frac{1}{0.1101} \\approx 9.083$\n$q_{vib, \\text{approx}} = \\frac{4000}{466.5} \\approx 8.575$\nDifference = $|9.083 - 8.575| = 0.508$\nPercentage difference = $(0.508 / 8.575) \\times 100\\% \\approx 5.92\\%$\n\nIf $T = 4500 \\mathrm{~K}$:\n$\\Theta_v/T = 466.5 / 4500 = 0.1037$\n$e^{-\\Theta_v/T} = e^{-0.1037} \\approx 0.9015$\n$q_{vib} = \\frac{1}{1 - 0.9015} = \\frac{1}{0.0985} \\approx 10.152$\n$q_{vib, \\text{approx}} = \\frac{4500}{466.5} \\approx 9.646$\nDifference = $|10.152 - 9.646| = 0.506$\nPercentage difference = $(0.506 / 9.646) \\times 100\\% \\approx 5.25\\%$\n\nIf $T = 5000 \\mathrm{~K}$:\n$\\Theta_v/T = 466.5 / 5000 = 0.0933$\n$e^{-\\Theta_v/T} = e^{-0.0933} \\approx 0.9109$\n$q_{vib} = \\frac{1}{1 - 0.9109} = \\frac{1}{0.0891} \\approx 11.223$\n$q_{vib, \\text{approx}} = \\frac{5000}{466.5} \\approx 10.718$\nDifference = $|11.223 - 10.718| = 0.505$\nPercentage difference = $(0.505 / 10.718) \\times 100\\% \\approx 4.71\\%$\n\nAt $T = 5000 \\mathrm{~K}$, the percentage difference is approximately 4.71%, which is within 5 per cent.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{I}$.",
