    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6623",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Draw one card at random from a standard deck of cards. The sample space $S$ is the collection of the 52 cards. Assume that the probability set function assigns $1 / 52$ to each of the 52 outcomes. Let\n$$\n\\begin{{aligned}}\nA & =\\{{x: x \\text {{ is a jack, queen, or king }}\\}}, \\\\\nB & =\\{{x: x \\text {{ is a }} 9,10, \\text {{ or jack and }} x \\text {{ is red }}\\}}, \\\\\nC & =\\{{x: x \\text {{ is a club }}\\}}, \\\\\nD & =\\{{x: x \\text {{ is a diamond, a heart, or a spade }}\\}} .\n\\end{{aligned}}\n$$\nFind $P(A)$\n\nOptions: \nA. $\\frac{{14}}{{52}}$\nB. $\\frac{{12}}{{52}}$\nC. $\\frac{{13}}{{52}}$\nD. $\\frac{{15}}{{52}}$\nE. $\\frac{{10}}{{52}}$\nF. $\\frac{{7}}{{52}}$\nG. $\\frac{{11}}{{52}}$\nH. $\\frac{{9}}{{52}}$\nI. $\\frac{{8}}{{52}}$\nJ. $\\frac{{16}}{{52}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find $P(A)$, we need to determine the number of outcomes in event $A$ and divide it by the total number of outcomes in the sample space $S$.\nEvent $A$ is the set of cards that are a jack, queen, or king. In a standard deck of 52 cards, there are four suits: hearts, diamonds, clubs, and spades. Each suit has one jack, one queen, and one king.\nTherefore, the number of jacks is 4, the number of queens is 4, and the number of kings is 4.\nThe total number of cards in event $A$ is the sum of the number of jacks, queens, and kings: $4 + 4 + 4 = 12$.\nThe sample space $S$ has 52 cards.\nThe probability of event $A$, $P(A)$, is the number of outcomes in $A$ divided by the total number of outcomes in $S$.\nSo, $P(A) = \\frac{\\text{Number of cards in A}}{\\text{Total number of cards in S}} = \\frac{12}{52}$.\n\nComparing this probability with the given options:\nA. $\\frac{14}{52}$\nB. $\\frac{12}{52}$\nC. $\\frac{13}{52}$\nD. $\\frac{15}{52}$\nE. $\\frac{10}{52}$\nF. $\\frac{7}{52}$\nG. $\\frac{11}{52}$\nH. $\\frac{9}{52}$\nI. $\\frac{8}{52}$\nJ. $\\frac{16}{52}$\n\nThe calculated probability $\\frac{12}{52}$ matches option B.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
