      "generated_answer": "To find $F_{0.01}(8,4)$, we need to look up the F-distribution critical value for a cumulative probability of $0.01$ with 8 degrees of freedom in the numerator and 4 degrees of freedom in the denominator. This value represents the point below which 1% of the distribution lies. Using an F-distribution table or statistical software, we find the value that corresponds to these parameters.\n\nConsulting an F-distribution table or using a calculator for $F_{0.01}(8,4)$:\nFor a cumulative probability of 0.01 (which corresponds to a right-tail probability of $1 - 0.01 = 0.99$), with numerator degrees of freedom $v_1 = 8$ and denominator degrees of freedom $v_2 = 4$, the F-value is approximately 16.30.\n\nComparing this value to the given options:\nA. 16.30\nB. 15.97\nC. 9.22\nD. 18.45\nE. 17.10\nF. 14.80\nG. 13.60\nH. 10.75\nI. 11.34\nJ. 12.50\n\nThe closest value is 16.30.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{A}$.",
