      "generated_answer": "The riddle describes an object with 2 faces, no vertices, and the ability to roll.\n\nLet's analyze the options:\n*   **A. hexagonal prism, D. prism, F. rectangular prism, G. pentagonal prism, H. cube:** These all have more than 2 faces and many vertices.\n*   **B. torus:** A torus has no faces and no vertices.\n*   **C. cone:** A cone has 2 faces (a circular base and a curved surface) but also has one vertex (the apex).\n*   **E. sphere:** A sphere has no faces and no vertices.\n*   **I. cylinder:** A cylinder has 2 flat circular faces (top and bottom) and a curved surface that can be thought of as a single face. It has no vertices. It can also roll.\n*   **J. pyramid:** A pyramid has more than 2 faces and has a vertex (the apex).\n\nTherefore, a cylinder fits all the clues: it has two circular faces, no vertices, and can roll.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{I}$",
