  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7086",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the number pattern 5, 9, 13, 17, 21, 25, 29. Which rule could have been used to make the pattern?\n\nOptions: \nA. Start with 5. Subtract 4 each time to get the next number.\nB. Start with 5. Add 4 each time to get the next number.\nC. Start with 5. Add 5 each time to get the next number.\nD. Start with 0. Add 5 each time to get the next number.\nE. Start with 9. Subtract 4 each time to get the next number.\nF. Start with 1. Add 4 each time to get the next number.\nG. Start with 0. Add 4 each time to get the next number.\nH. Start with 0. Add 3 each time to get the next number.\nI. Start with 5. Add 3 each time to get the next number.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let's analyze the given number pattern: 5, 9, 13, 17, 21, 25, 29.\nWe observe the difference between consecutive numbers:\n9 - 5 = 4\n13 - 9 = 4\n17 - 13 = 4\n21 - 17 = 4\n25 - 21 = 4\n29 - 25 = 4\nThe difference between each consecutive term is consistently 4. This means we are adding 4 each time. The pattern starts with the number 5.\n\nNow let's evaluate the given options:\nA. Start with 5. Subtract 4 each time to get the next number. (This would yield 5, 1, -3, ...) - Incorrect.\nB. Start with 5. Add 4 each time to get the next number. (This would yield 5, 9, 13, 17, 21, 25, 29, ...) - Correct.\nC. Start with 5. Add 5 each time to get the next number. (This would yield 5, 10, 15, ...) - Incorrect.\nD. Start with 0. Add 5 each time to get the next number. (This would yield 0, 5, 10, ...) - Incorrect.\nE. Start with 9. Subtract 4 each time to get the next number. (This would yield 9, 5, 1, ...) - Incorrect.\nF. Start with 1. Add 4 each time to get the next number. (This would yield 1, 5, 9, 13, ...) - Incorrect, as the pattern starts with 5.\nG. Start with 0. Add 4 each time to get the next number. (This would yield 0, 4, 8, 12, ...) - Incorrect.\nH. Start with 0. Add 3 each time to get the next number. (This would yield 0, 3, 6, 9, ...) - Incorrect.\nI. Start with 5. Add 3 each time to get the next number. (This would yield 5, 8, 11, ...) - Incorrect.\n\nThe rule that accurately generates the given pattern is to start with 5 and add 4 each time.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 274,
        "output_tokens": 538,
        "total_tokens": 812
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
