    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine which set of integers is in order from least to greatest, we need to compare the values of the integers. Negative numbers are always less than positive numbers. Among negative numbers, the one with the larger absolute value is smaller.\n\nLet's examine each option:\n\nA. $11, -9, 7, -6, -3$\nThis is not ordered because $11$ is greater than $-9$.\n\nB. $7, 11, -6, -3, -9$\nThis is not ordered because $7$ and $11$ are positive, and then negative numbers follow. Also, $-6$ is greater than $-9$.\n\nC. $-3, 7, -9, -6, 11$\nThis is not ordered because $7$ is greater than $-9$.\n\nD. $-6, -3, 7, 11, -9$\nThis is not ordered because $11$ is greater than $-9$.\n\nE. $-9, -3, 7, 11, -6$\nThis is not ordered because $11$ is greater than $-6$.\n\nF. $-3, -6, 7, 11, -9$\nThis is not ordered because $-3$ is greater than $-6$, and $11$ is greater than $-9$.\n\nG. $-9, 7, -6, -3, 11$\nThis is not ordered because $7$ is greater than $-6$.\n\nH. $-9, -6, -3, 7, 11$\nLet's check this option. All the negative numbers are placed before the positive numbers. We compare the negative numbers from smallest to largest: $-9 < -6 < -3$. Then we compare the positive numbers from smallest to largest: $7 < 11$. Therefore, the entire set is ordered from least to greatest.\n\nI. $11, 7, -3, -6, -9$\nThis is not ordered because $11$ is greater than $7$.\n\nJ. $7, -9, -6, -3, 11$\nThis is not ordered because $7$ is greater than $-9$.\n\nThe set of integers in order from least to greatest is $-9, -6, -3, 7, 11$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{H}$.",
