    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6662",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which group of numbers is in order from least to greatest?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.6 1.0 0.25\nB. 0.25 1.6 1.0\nC. 1.0 1.6 0.25\nD. 1.6 0.25 1.6\nE. 1.0 0.25 0.25\nF. 1.6 0.25 1.0\nG. 0.25 1.0 1.6\nH. 1.0 0.25 1.6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The question asks to identify the group of numbers ordered from least to greatest. We need to compare the values in each option.\n\nOption A: 1.6, 1.0, 0.25. In this case, 1.0 is less than 1.6, and 0.25 is less than 1.0. This is not in order from least to greatest.\nOption B: 0.25, 1.6, 1.0. Here, 1.6 is greater than 0.25, but 1.0 is less than 1.6. This is not in order from least to greatest.\nOption C: 1.0, 1.6, 0.25. Here, 1.6 is greater than 1.0, but 0.25 is less than 1.0. This is not in order from least to greatest.\nOption D: 1.6, 0.25, 1.6. Here, 0.25 is less than 1.6. This is not in order from least to greatest.\nOption E: 1.0, 0.25, 0.25. Here, 0.25 is less than 1.0. This is not in order from least to greatest.\nOption F: 1.6, 0.25, 1.0. Here, 0.25 is less than 1.6. This is not in order from least to greatest.\nOption G: 0.25, 1.0, 1.6. Here, 0.25 is the smallest number. 1.0 is greater than 0.25. 1.6 is greater than 1.0. Thus, these numbers are in order from least to greatest.\nOption H: 1.0, 0.25, 1.6. Here, 0.25 is less than 1.0. This is not in order from least to greatest.\n\nTherefore, option G is the only one where the numbers are listed in increasing order.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{G}$.",
