  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6979",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The weekly milk order for the Tranquility Inn includes 40 gallons of low-fat milk and 15 gallons of chocolate milk. What is the ratio of the number of low-fat gallons to chocolate gallons in the Tranquility Inn’s weekly milk order?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5:03\nB. 8:04\nC. 8:05\nD. 2:01\nE. 3:01\nF. 8:03\nG. 7:03\nH. 6:03\nI. 4:01\nJ. 5:01\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The problem asks for the ratio of the number of low-fat gallons to chocolate gallons.\nNumber of low-fat gallons = 40\nNumber of chocolate gallons = 15\n\nThe ratio of low-fat gallons to chocolate gallons is 40:15.\nTo simplify the ratio, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 40 and 15.\nThe factors of 40 are 1, 2, 4, 5, 8, 10, 20, 40.\nThe factors of 15 are 1, 3, 5, 15.\nThe GCD of 40 and 15 is 5.\n\nDivide both parts of the ratio by the GCD:\n40 / 5 = 8\n15 / 5 = 3\n\nSo, the simplified ratio is 8:3.\n\nNow let's compare this with the given options:\nA. 5:03\nB. 8:04\nC. 8:05\nD. 2:01\nE. 3:01\nF. 8:03\nG. 7:03\nH. 6:03\nI. 4:01\nJ. 5:01\n\nThe calculated ratio is 8:3, which matches option F.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{F}$",
      "success": true,
