      "generated_answer": "To find another way to express the number of days Katie will miss, we can consider that she will miss 5 days of work each week for 3 weeks. The expression \\(5 + 5 + 5 + 5 + 5\\) counts each of the 5 workdays in the 3 weeks, thus the correct option is F, which represents adding 5 days a total of 5 times. \n\nSo, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).",
