  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7357",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compute the real integral $I=\\int_{{-\\infty}}^{{\\infty}} 1/(x^2 + 1)^2 dx$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 6.28\nB. 5.55\nC. 3.67\nD. 2.78\nE. 3.14\nF. 2.46\nG. 1.57\nH. 4.67\nI. 1.23\nJ. 0.78\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To compute the integral $I=\\int_{{-\\infty}}^{{\\infty}} 1/(x^2 + 1)^2 dx$, we can use a contour integration method or trigonometric substitution.\n\nUsing trigonometric substitution with $x = \\tan \\theta$, $dx = \\sec^2 \\theta d\\theta$.\nWhen $x \\to \\infty$, $\\theta \\to \\pi/2$. When $x \\to -\\infty$, $\\theta \\to -\\pi/2$.\n$x^2 + 1 = \\tan^2 \\theta + 1 = \\sec^2 \\theta$.\nSo, $(x^2 + 1)^2 = (\\sec^2 \\theta)^2 = \\sec^4 \\theta$.\nThe integral becomes:\n$I = \\int_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2} \\frac{1}{\\sec^4 \\theta} \\sec^2 \\theta d\\theta = \\int_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2} \\frac{1}{\\sec^2 \\theta} d\\theta = \\int_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2} \\cos^2 \\theta d\\theta$.\n\nUsing the identity $\\cos^2 \\theta = \\frac{1 + \\cos(2\\theta)}{2}$:\n$I = \\int_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2} \\frac{1 + \\cos(2\\theta)}{2} d\\theta = \\frac{1}{2} \\int_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2} (1 + \\cos(2\\theta)) d\\theta$.\n$I = \\frac{1}{2} \\left[ \\theta + \\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2\\theta) \\right]_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2}$.\n$I = \\frac{1}{2} \\left[ (\\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}\\sin(\\pi)) - (-\\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}\\sin(-\\pi)) \\right]$.\n$I = \\frac{1}{2} \\left[ (\\frac{\\pi}{2} + 0) - (-\\frac{\\pi}{2} + 0) \\right]$.\n$I = \\frac{1}{2} \\left[ \\frac{\\pi}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right] = \\frac{1}{2} [\\pi] = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$.\n\nNow we approximate the value of $\\pi/2$.\n$\\pi \\approx 3.14159$.\n$I = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\approx \\frac{3.14159}{2} \\approx 1.570795$.\n\nComparing this value to the given options:\nA. 6.28\nB. 5.55\nC. 3.67\nD. 2.78\nE. 3.14\nF. 2.46\nG. 1.57\nH. 4.67\nI. 1.23\nJ. 0.78\n\nThe value 1.57 is closest to our computed value.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{G}$.",
