    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6698",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: suppose F(x,y,z)=0. What is $\\frac{{\\partial x}}{{\\partial y}} \\frac{{\\partial y}}{{\\partial z}} \\frac{{\\partial z}}{{\\partial x}}$?\n\nOptions: \nA. -2.0\nB. 2.0\nC. -0.5\nD. 0\nE. 1.5\nF. 1.0\nG. Undefined\nH. -1.0\nI. 0.5\nJ. 3.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The problem involves implicit differentiation of a function of three variables. When $F(x,y,z)=0$, we can treat $x$, $y$, and $z$ as implicitly related. Using the chain rule for total differentials, we have\n$dF = \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial x}}dx + \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial y}}dy + \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial z}}dz = 0$.\n\nWe can find the partial derivatives using the implicit function theorem.\n$\\frac{{\\partial x}}{{\\partial y}} = - \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial y}} / \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial x}}$\n$\\frac{{\\partial y}}{{\\partial z}} = - \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial z}} / \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial y}}$\n$\\frac{{\\partial z}}{{\\partial x}} = - \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial x}} / \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial z}}$\n\nMultiplying these three together, we get:\n$\\frac{{\\partial x}}{{\\partial y}} \\frac{{\\partial y}}{{\\partial z}} \\frac{{\\partial z}}{{\\partial x}} = \\left( - \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial y}} / \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial x}} \\right) \\left( - \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial z}} / \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial y}} \\right) \\left( - \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial x}} / \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial z}} \\right)$\n$= \\left( -1 \\right)^3 \\left( \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial y}} \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial z}} \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial x}} \\right) / \\left( \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial x}} \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial y}} \\frac{{\\partial F}}{{\\partial z}} \\right)$\n$= -1$.\n\nThis result is a general property of implicitly defined functions. Assuming the partial derivatives of F with respect to x, y, and z are non-zero, the product of these cyclic partial derivatives is -1.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{H}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 171,
        "output_tokens": 477,
        "total_tokens": 648
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
