    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6595",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is \\lim_{{x \\to 0}} (csc(x) - cot(x))?\n\nOptions: \nA. -1/2\nB. Undefined\nC. 1/2\nD. 1\nE. 0\nF. -1\nG. 2\nH. -2\nI. 3\nJ. Infinity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "openai/gpt-4o-mini",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find \\(\\lim_{{x \\to 0}} (csc(x) - cot(x))\\), we can rewrite it as \\(\\lim_{{x \\to 0}} \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sin(x)} - \\frac{\\cos(x)}{\\sin(x)}\\right) = \\lim_{{x \\to 0}} \\frac{1 - \\cos(x)}{\\sin(x)}\\). As \\(x \\to 0\\), \\(1 - \\cos(x) \\approx \\frac{x^2}{2}\\) and \\(\\sin(x) \\approx x\\), leading to \\(\\lim_{{x \\to 0}} \\frac{\\frac{x^2}{2}}{x} = \\lim_{{x \\to 0}} \\frac{x}{2} = 0\\). Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).",
