    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a\\geq 0, we define $S_a={{x | dist(x, S) \\leq a}}$, where $dist(x,S)=inf_{{y\\in S}}||x-y||$. Suppose S is convex. Is S_a convex? Return 1 for yes and 0 for no.\n\nOptions: \nA. Undefined\nB. 0.0\nC. None of the above\nD. 1.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The set $S_a$ is the set of all points $x$ whose distance to the set $S$ is less than or equal to $a$. This is equivalent to taking the Minkowski sum of $S$ with a closed ball of radius $a$ centered at the origin. Since $S$ is convex and a closed ball is convex, their Minkowski sum is also convex. Therefore, $S_a$ is convex.\n\nThe correct answer is D. 1.0.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
