    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7177",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A talk show host recently reported that in response to his on-air question, 82% of the more than 2500 e-mail messages received through his publicized address supported the death penalty for anyone convicted of selling drugs to children. What does this show?\n\nOptions: \nA. The survey is biased because it only includes listeners who have access to email.\nB. The survey would have been more meaningful if he had used a control group.\nC. The survey is accurate as it includes a large number of responses.\nD. The survey would have been more meaningful if he had picked a random sample of the 2500 listeners who responded.\nE. The survey is valid because it represents the opinion of the show's listeners.\nF. The survey would have been more meaningful if he had included listeners who disagreed with his viewpoint.\nG. The survey is meaningless because of voluntary response bias.\nH. The survey shows that the majority of the host's listeners support the death penalty for drug dealers.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "This question describes a voluntary response sample, which is inherently biased. Listeners who are compelled to respond are more likely to share strong opinions, and those who have access to email may not be representative of the general population or even the show's entire audience. Therefore, the survey results are not necessarily accurate or representative of a larger group.\n\nThe most likely correct answer is **G**.\n\nExplanation:\nA voluntary response survey, where participants self-select to respond, is prone to bias. This means the results are unlikely to be representative of the broader population or even the show's entire listener base. Having a large number of responses does not automatically make a biased survey accurate.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{G}$.",
