    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7446",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When the graph of a certain function $f(x)$ is shifted $2$ units to the right and stretched vertically by a factor of $2$ (meaning that all $y$-coordinates are doubled), the resulting figure is identical to the original graph. Given that $f(0)=0.1$, what is $f(10)$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.01\nB. 32\nC. 3.2\nD. 5\nE. 1\nF. 0.2\nG. 0.5\nH. 2\nI. 10\nJ. 20\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $g(x)$ be the function obtained by shifting $f(x)$ 2 units to the right and stretching vertically by a factor of 2.\nShifting $f(x)$ 2 units to the right gives $f(x-2)$.\nStretching $f(x-2)$ vertically by a factor of 2 gives $2f(x-2)$.\nSo, $g(x) = 2f(x-2)$.\nThe problem states that the resulting figure is identical to the original graph, which means $g(x) = f(x)$ for all $x$.\nTherefore, we have $f(x) = 2f(x-2)$ for all $x$.\nWe are given that $f(0) = 0.1$. We want to find $f(10)$.\nWe can use the relation $f(x) = 2f(x-2)$ to find $f(10)$.\n$f(10) = 2f(10-2) = 2f(8)$\n$f(8) = 2f(8-2) = 2f(6)$\n$f(6) = 2f(6-2) = 2f(4)$\n$f(4) = 2f(4-2) = 2f(2)$\n$f(2) = 2f(2-2) = 2f(0)$\nSo, $f(10) = 2f(8) = 2(2f(6)) = 4f(6) = 4(2f(4)) = 8f(4) = 8(2f(2)) = 16f(2) = 16(2f(0)) = 32f(0)$.\nGiven $f(0) = 0.1$, we have $f(10) = 32 \\times 0.1 = 3.2$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$.",
