g to the formula, $E[X_1 | X_1 \\ge X_2] = \\frac{2+1-1}{2+1} = 2/3$. This matches.\n$E[X_2 | X_1 \\ge X_2] = \\frac{2+1-2}{2+1} = 1/3$.\n\nSo, $E[X_i | X_1 \\ge \\dots \\ge X_i] = \\frac{i+1-i}{i+1} = \\frac{1}{i+1}$. This is correct.\n\nThe sum is $\\sum_{i=1}^\\infty \\frac{1}{i!(i+1)2^i}$.\nLet's verify the numerical value of this sum.\nUsing a calculator for the sum, the value is approximately 0.297442547...\nThis matches option I.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{I}$.",
