    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6466",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let V be the real vector space of all real 2 x 3 matrices, and let W be the real vector space of all real 4 x 1 column vectors. If T is a linear transformation from V onto W, what is the dimension of the subspace kernel of T?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 3\nC. 9\nD. 4\nE. 2\nF. 0\nG. 7\nH. 6\nI. 1\nJ. 8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The space V has dimension $2 \\times 3 = 6$. The space W has dimension $4 \\times 1 = 4$. Since T is a linear transformation from V onto W, the image of T is W, so the dimension of the image is 4. By the rank-nullity theorem, the dimension of V is equal to the dimension of the kernel of T plus the dimension of the image of T. Therefore, $6 = \\dim(\\text{ker}(T)) + 4$, which implies $\\dim(\\text{ker}(T)) = 6 - 4 = 2$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
