    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: suppose a,b,c,\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma are six real numbers with a^2+b^2+c^2>0.  In addition, $a=b*cos(\\gamma)+c*cos(\\beta), b=c*cos(\\alpha)+a*cos(\\gamma), c=a*cos(\\beta)+b*cos(\\alpha)$. What is the value of $cos^2(\\alpha)+cos^2(\\beta)+cos^2(\\gamma)+2*cos(\\alpha)*cos(\\beta)*cos(\\gamma)? return the numeric.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.5\nB. 0.0\nC. 2.0\nD. 1.0\nE. -0.5\nF. 1.5\nG. -1.0\nH. 2.5\nI. 3.0\nJ. 0.25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given equations are a system of linear equations in terms of a, b, and c. Rearranging the terms, we get:\n$a - b\\cos(\\gamma) - c\\cos(\\beta) = 0$\n$-a\\cos(\\gamma) + b - c\\cos(\\alpha) = 0$\n$-a\\cos(\\beta) - b\\cos(\\alpha) + c = 0$\n\nThis system can be written in matrix form as:\n$$\n\\begin{pmatrix}\n1 & -\\cos(\\gamma) & -\\cos(\\beta) \\\\\n-\\cos(\\gamma) & 1 & -\\cos(\\alpha) \\\\\n-\\cos(\\beta) & -\\cos(\\alpha) & 1\n\\end{pmatrix}\n\\begin{pmatrix}\na \\\\\nb \\\\\nc\n\\end{pmatrix}\n=\n\\begin{pmatrix}\n0 \\\\\n0 \\\\\n0\n\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\nFor a non-trivial solution (i.e., $a^2+b^2+c^2>0$), the determinant of the coefficient matrix must be zero.\nThe determinant is:\n$1(1 - \\cos^2(\\alpha)) - (-\\cos(\\gamma))(-\\cos(\\gamma) - \\cos(\\beta)\\cos(\\alpha)) + (-\\cos(\\beta))(\\cos(\\gamma)\\cos(\\alpha) - (-\\cos(\\beta)))$\n$= 1 - \\cos^2(\\alpha) - \\cos^2(\\gamma) - \\cos(\\beta)\\cos(\\gamma)\\cos(\\alpha) - \\cos(\\beta)\\cos(\\gamma)\\cos(\\alpha) - \\cos^2(\\beta)$\n$= 1 - \\cos^2(\\alpha) - \\cos^2(\\beta) - \\cos^2(\\gamma) - 2\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta)\\cos(\\gamma)$\n\nSetting the determinant to zero:\n$1 - \\cos^2(\\alpha) - \\cos^2(\\beta) - \\cos^2(\\gamma) - 2\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta)\\cos(\\gamma) = 0$\nRearranging this equation to find the value of the expression asked for in the question:\n$\\cos^2(\\alpha) + \\cos^2(\\beta) + \\cos^2(\\gamma) + 2\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta)\\cos(\\gamma) = 1$\n\nThe value of $cos^2(\\alpha)+cos^2(\\beta)+cos^2(\\gamma)+2*cos(\\alpha)*cos(\\beta)*cos(\\gamma)$ is 1.0.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
