    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_6952",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the value of the inflection point of f(x) =(10 ln(x))/(x^2)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.000\nB. 1.587\nC. 0.693\nD. 1.203\nE. 3.014\nF. 2.718\nG. 4.000\nH. 3.142\nI. 1.000\nJ. 2.301\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the inflection point, we need to find the second derivative of the function and set it to zero.\nFirst, find the first derivative:\n$f'(x) = \\frac{d}{dx} \\left( \\frac{10 \\ln(x)}{x^2} \\right) = 10 \\frac{\\frac{1}{x} x^2 - \\ln(x) 2x}{(x^2)^2} = 10 \\frac{x - 2x \\ln(x)}{x^4} = 10 \\frac{1 - 2 \\ln(x)}{x^3}$\n\nNext, find the second derivative:\n$f''(x) = \\frac{d}{dx} \\left( 10 \\frac{1 - 2 \\ln(x)}{x^3} \\right) = 10 \\frac{(-2 \\frac{1}{x}) x^3 - (1 - 2 \\ln(x)) 3x^2}{(x^3)^2}$\n$f''(x) = 10 \\frac{-2x^2 - 3x^2 + 6x^2 \\ln(x)}{x^6} = 10 \\frac{-5x^2 + 6x^2 \\ln(x)}{x^6} = 10 \\frac{-5 + 6 \\ln(x)}{x^4}$\n\nTo find the inflection point, set $f''(x) = 0$:\n$10 \\frac{-5 + 6 \\ln(x)}{x^4} = 0$\n$-5 + 6 \\ln(x) = 0$\n$6 \\ln(x) = 5$\n$\\ln(x) = \\frac{5}{6}$\n$x = e^{\\frac{5}{6}}$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the value of $e^{\\frac{5}{6}}$ and compare it to the given options.\n$e^{\\frac{5}{6}} \\approx e^{0.8333}$\nUsing a calculator, $e^{5/6} \\approx 2.30193$.\n\nComparing this value to the given options:\nA. 2.000\nB. 1.587\nC. 0.693\nD. 1.203\nE. 3.014\nF. 2.718\nG. 4.000\nH. 3.142\nI. 1.000\nJ. 2.301\n\nThe closest option to 2.30193 is 2.301.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{J}$.",
