st half string of length 3 from {I, S, P}, with the constraint that the counts of each letter in this string (when doubled) do not exceed the available counts.\n$n_I' \\le 2$, $n_S' \\le 2$, $n_P' \\le 1$.\nThe sum of counts in the string of length 3 is 3.\nPossible count combinations (nI, nS, nP) summing to 3:\n- (2, 1, 0): II S. Permutations: IIS, ISI, SII. (3 arrangements). Constraints satisfied.\n  e.g., IIS -> IIS M SII. Needs 4 I, 2 S. Possible.\n- (2, 0, 1): II P. Permutations: IIP, IPI, PII. (3 arrangements). Constraints satisfied.\n  e.g., IIP -> IIP M PII. Needs 4 I, 2 P. Possible.\n- (1, 2, 0): I S S. Permutations: ISS, SIS, SSI. (3 arrangements). Constraints satisfied.\n  e.g., ISS -> ISS M SSI. Needs 2 I, 4 S. Possible.\n- (0, 2, 1): S S P. Permutations: SSP, SPS, PSS. (3 arrangements). Constraints satisfied.\n  e.g., SSP -> SSP M PSS. Needs 4 S, 2 P. Possible.\n- (1, 1, 1): I S P. Permutations: ISP, IPS, SIP, SPI, PIS, PSI. (6 arrangements). Constraints satisfied.\n  e.g., ISP -> ISP M PSI. Needs 2 I, 2 S, 2 P. Possible.\nTotal = 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 6 = 18. This is correct.\n\nLet's double check the calculation for length 9.\nPalindrome is $c_1 c_2 c_3 c_4 M c_4 c_3 c_2 c_1$.\nFirst half string length 4, from {I, S, P}.\nConstraints: $n_I' \\le 2$, $n_S' \\le 2$, $n_P' \\le 1$.\nSum of counts in the string of length 4 is 4.\nPossible count combinations (nI, nS, nP) summing to 4:\n- (2, 2, 0): II S S. Arrangements: $\\frac{4!}{2!2!} = 6$. Constraints satisfied.\n  e.g., IISS -> IISSMSSII. Needs 4 I, 4 S. Possible.\n- (2, 1, 1): II S P. Arrangements: $\\frac{4!}{2!1!1!} = 12$. Constraints satisfied.\n  e.g., IIPS -> IIPSMSPII. Needs 4 I, 2 S, 2 P. Possible.\n- (1, 2, 1): I S S P. Arrangements: $\\frac{4!}{1!2!1!} = 12$. Constraints satisfied.\n  e.g., ISSP -> ISSPMPSII. Needs 2 I, 4 S, 2 P. Possible.\nTotal = 6 + 12 + 12 = 30. This is correct.\n\nLet's consider if there are any palindromes of even length containing M.\nFor an even length palindrome, say $c_1