    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Statement 1 | Q is an extension field of Z_2. Statement 2 | Every non-constant polynomial over a field has a zero in some extension field.\n\nOptions: \nA. Not Applicable, False\nB. False, True\nC. True, Not Applicable\nD. True, False\nE. False, False\nF. True, Not Determinable\nG. True, True\nH. False, Not Applicable\nI. Not Applicable, Not Applicable\nJ. Not Applicable, True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let's analyze each statement.\n\nStatement 1: \"Q is an extension field of Z_2.\"\nA field $\\mathbb{Q}$ is the field of rational numbers, and $\\mathbb{Z}_2$ is the field of integers modulo 2. The elements of $\\mathbb{Z}_2$ are $\\{0, 1\\}$. For $\\mathbb{Q}$ to be an extension field of $\\mathbb{Z}_2$, $\\mathbb{Z}_2$ must be a subfield of $\\mathbb{Q}$. However, the characteristic of $\\mathbb{Q}$ is 0, while the characteristic of $\\mathbb{Z}_2$ is 2. In an extension field, the characteristic of the base field must be the same as the characteristic of the extension field. Since the characteristics are different, $\\mathbb{Q}$ cannot be an extension field of $\\mathbb{Z}_2$. Therefore, Statement 1 is False.\n\nStatement 2: \"Every non-constant polynomial over a field has a zero in some extension field.\"\nThis statement is a fundamental result in field theory, often referred to as the \"extension property\" or a consequence of the algebraic closure theorem. For any field $F$, there exists an algebraic closure $\\bar{F}$ which is an extension field of $F$. It is a known theorem that every non-constant polynomial over $F$ has a root (a zero) in its algebraic closure $\\bar{F}$. Therefore, Statement 2 is True.\n\nBased on our analysis, Statement 1 is False and Statement 2 is True.\n\nLooking at the options:\nA. Not Applicable, False\nB. False, True\nC. True, Not Applicable\nD. True, False\nE. False, False\nF. True, Not Determinable\nG. True, True\nH. False, Not Applicable\nI. Not Applicable, Not Applicable\nJ. Not Applicable, True\n\nThe option that matches \"False, True\" is B.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
