    "global index": "MMLUPro_physics_7887",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the value of (I / I_0) for the first diagonal maximum of the Fraunhoferdiffraction pattern of a circular aperture.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.145\nB. 0.215\nC. 0.155\nD. 0.125\nE. 0.175\nF. 0.165\nG. 0.185\nH. 0.235\nI. 0.205\nJ. 0.195\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Fraunhofer diffraction pattern of a circular aperture is described by the Airy disk. The intensity distribution in the far field is given by $I(\\theta) = I_0 \\left(\\frac{2J_1(ka\\sin\\theta)}{ka\\sin\\theta}\\right)^2$, where $I_0$ is the central intensity, $J_1$ is the Bessel function of the first kind of order 1, $k$ is the wave number, and $a$ is the radius of the aperture. The minima of the diffraction pattern occur when $ka\\sin\\theta$ is a root of $J_1(x) = 0$. The first minimum occurs at the first non-zero root of $J_1(x)$, which is approximately $x = 3.8317$. The central maximum has an intensity of $I_0$. The first diagonal maximum, which is the peak intensity of the first bright ring surrounding the central maximum, is approximately $0.175 I_0$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 180,
        "output_tokens": 227,
        "total_tokens": 407
