    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The question asks for the number of allowed values of the magnetic quantum number $m_l$ for an electron in the state with orbital angular momentum quantum number $l = 2$. The allowed values of $m_l$ are integers ranging from $-l$ to $+l$, including 0. Therefore, for $l=2$, the possible values of $m_l$ are -2, -1, 0, +1, +2. Counting these values, there are 5 possible values for $m_l$.\n\nThe values of $m_l$ for $l=2$ are:\n$m_l = -2, -1, 0, 1, 2$\n\nThe number of possible values is $2l + 1$.\nFor $l = 2$, the number of allowed values of $m_l$ is $2(2) + 1 = 4 + 1 = 5$.\n\nThe options given are:\nA. 8\nB. 5\nC. 3\nD. 2\nE. 6\nF. 9\nG. 4\nH. 1\nI. 7\nJ. 0\n\nComparing our result to the options, the correct answer is 5, which corresponds to option B.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
