      "generated_answer": "The resultant force of two vectors is the vector sum of the individual forces. The magnitude of the resultant force can range from the difference of the magnitudes of the two vectors to the sum of their magnitudes. In this case, the minimum resultant force is $4 N - 3 N = 1 N$, and the maximum resultant force is $4 N + 3 N = 7 N$. Therefore, any resultant force between 1 N and 7 N (inclusive) is possible. Looking at the options, 5 N is within this range. A detailed analysis shows that forces of 3 N and 4 N at a 90-degree angle result in a 5 N resultant.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{I}$.",
