    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: According to Hooke’s law, if you hang by a tree branch and note how much it bends, then hanging with twice the weight produces\n\nOptions: \nA. three times the bend.\nB. twice the bend.\nC. four times the bend if the branch doesn’t break.\nD. no bend at all.\nE. a bend that is unpredictable.\nF. half the bend.\nG. a bend that is proportional to the square root of the weight.\nH. 4 times the bend.\nI. a bend that decreases with increased weight.\nJ. the same bend if the branch doesn’t break.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
