    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following gives the total spin quantum number of the electrons in the ground state of neutral nitrogen (Z = 7)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1\nB. 5/2\nC. 3\nD. 2\nE. 4 1/2\nF. 1/2\nG. 0\nH. 2 1/2\nI. 4\nJ. 3/2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "openai/gpt-4o-mini",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the total spin quantum number of the electrons in ground state neutral nitrogen (Z = 7), we first note that nitrogen has 7 electrons, which fill the orbitals according to the Aufbau principle. The electron configuration is 1s² 2s² 2p³. In the 2p orbital, there are three electrons that occupy the three available p orbitals and tend to have parallel spins (hund's rule). This results in a total spin of \\( \\frac{3}{2} \\) (one spin-up in each of the three p orbitals), making the total spin quantum number:\n\n\\(\\boxed{J}\\)",
