    "global index": "MMLUPro_physics_8719",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The quantum efficiency of a photon detector is 0.1. If 100 photons are sent into the detector, one after the other, the detector will detect photons\n\nOptions: \nA. an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 5\nB. an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 3\nC. an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 0.1\nD. an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 1\nE. an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 6\nF. an average of 5 times, with an rms deviation of about 2\nG. an average of 20 times, with an rms deviation of about 3\nH. an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 4\nI. an average of 15 times, with an rms deviation of about 4\nJ. an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The quantum efficiency (QE) is the probability that a single photon will be detected. In this case, QE = 0.1. If 100 photons are sent, the expected number of detected photons is $100 \\times 0.1 = 10$. The detection process for each photon is an independent Bernoulli trial, so the number of detected photons follows a binomial distribution with parameters $n=100$ and $p=0.1$. For a large number of trials, this can be approximated by a Poisson distribution with mean $\\lambda = np = 10$. The standard deviation of a Poisson distribution is $\\sqrt{\\lambda} = \\sqrt{10} \\approx 3.16$. The root-mean-square (rms) deviation is the same as the standard deviation.\n\nTherefore, the detector will detect photons an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 3.\n\nLooking at the options, option B states \"an average of 10 times, with an rms deviation of about 3\".\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
