      "generated_answer": "The beat frequency is the absolute difference between the frequencies of the two interfering sound waves. In this case, the frequencies are 500 Hz and 504 Hz. Therefore, the beat frequency is |504 Hz - 500 Hz| = 4 Hz. This pattern of constructive and destructive interference leads to a perceived fluctuation in loudness known as beats.\n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{F}.",
