    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If you lived on Venus what phases of the Earth would you see? (Assume your telescope can see through Venus’s thick clouds…)\n\nOptions: \nA. Waning crescent New Waxing crescent\nB. New Waxing crescent First quarter\nC. Full Waning crescent New\nD. Full moon only\nE. First quarter Waxing gibbous Full\nF. New only\nG. Waning gibbous New Waxing gibbous\nH. Waxing gibbous Full Waning gibbous\nI. Third quarter Waning crescent New\nJ. New first quarter full third quarter\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the phases of Earth visible from Venus, consider the relative orbits. Since Venus orbits the Sun inside Earth's orbit, Venus will be between Earth and the Sun and on the opposite side of the Sun from Earth. This creates similar phase geometry to what we see of Venus from Earth. Therefore, all phases of Earth, from new to full and back again, would be visible.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{J}$.",
