    "global index": "MMLUPro_physics_7982",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: From laboratory measurements we know that a particular spectral line formed by hydrogen appears at a wavelength of 486.1 nanometers (nm). The spectrum of a particular star shows the same hydrogen line appearing at a wavelength of 485.9 nm. What can we conclude?\n\nOptions: \nA. The star's brightness is fluctuating.\nB. The star's size is increasing.\nC. The star's size is decreasing.\nD. The star's temperature is constant.\nE. The star is getting hotter.\nF. The star is not moving.\nG. The star is rotating on its axis.\nH. The star is getting colder.\nI. The star is moving away from us.\nJ. The star is moving toward us.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
