    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What happens to the image formed by a concave mirror as the object is moved from far away to near the focal point?\n\nOptions: \nA. The image disappears as it moves toward the mirror.\nB. The image moves away from the mirror and gets taller.\nC. The image stays at the same distance from the mirror and gets shorter.\nD. The image moves toward the mirror and gets shorter.\nE. The image moves toward the mirror and gets taller.\nF. The image stays at the same distance from the mirror and gets taller.\nG. The image moves toward the mirror and stays the same height.\nH. The image flips upside down as it moves toward the mirror.\nI. The image moves away from the mirror and stays the same height.\nJ. The image moves away from the mirror and gets shorter.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "When an object is moved from far away towards the focal point of a concave mirror, the real image formed moves away from the mirror and increases in size. As the object approaches the focal point, the image distance increases, and the magnification increases, meaning the image gets taller. When the object is exactly at the focal point, the image is formed at infinity and is infinitely large and inverted (though we are considering the approach to the focal point).\n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{B}.",
