    "global index": "MathQA_1973",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: the average salary of all the workers in a workshop is rs . 8000 . the average salary of 9 technicians is rs . 18000 and the average salary of the rest is rs . 6000 . the total number of workers in the workshop is :\n\nOptions: \nA. 22\nB. 54\nC. 88\nD. 37\nE. 29\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let 'N' be the total number of workers in the workshop.\nLet 'T' be the number of technicians, so T = 9.\nLet 'R' be the number of rest of the workers, so R = N - 9.\n\nThe average salary of all workers is Rs. 8000. So, the total salary of all workers is 8000 * N.\nThe average salary of 9 technicians is Rs. 18000. So, the total salary of technicians is 18000 * 9 = 162000.\nThe average salary of the rest of the workers is Rs. 6000. So, the total salary of the rest of the workers is 6000 * R = 6000 * (N - 9).\n\nThe sum of the salaries of technicians and the rest of the workers must equal the total salary of all workers.\n162000 + 6000 * (N - 9) = 8000 * N\n162000 + 6000N - 54000 = 8000N\n108000 + 6000N = 8000N\n108000 = 8000N - 6000N\n108000 = 2000N\nN = 108000 / 2000\nN = 54\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$",
