      "generated_answer": "Let the father's current age be F and the son's current age be S.\nFrom the first statement, \"i was as old as you are at present at the time of your birth\", this means that when the son was born, the father's age was S.\nThe difference in their ages is F - S. This difference is also equal to S (the father's age when the son was born).\nSo, F - S = S, which simplifies to F = 2S.\n\nWe are given that the father's current age is 40, so F = 40.\nSubstitute F = 40 into the equation F = 2S:\n40 = 2S\nS = 40 / 2\nS = 20\n\nThe son's current age is 20 years.\nWe need to find the son's age 5 years back.\nSon's age 5 years back = Son's current age - 5\nSon's age 5 years back = 20 - 5 = 15.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$",
