  {
    "global index": "MathQA_2210",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: {{ - 10 , - 6 , - 5 , - 4 , - 2.5 , - 1 , 0 , 2.5 , 4 , 6 , 7 , 10 }} a number is to be selected at random from the set above . what is the probability that the number will be a solution to the equation ( x - 4 ) ( x + 9 ) ( 2 x + 5 ) = 0 ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 / 12\nB. 1 / 6\nC. 1 / 4\nD. 1 / 3\nE. 1 / 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The solutions to the equation $(x - 4)(x + 9)(2x + 5) = 0$ are found by setting each factor equal to zero.\n$x - 4 = 0 \\implies x = 4$\n$x + 9 = 0 \\implies x = -9$\n$2x + 5 = 0 \\implies 2x = -5 \\implies x = -2.5$\n\nThe set of numbers is $S = \\{-10, -6, -5, -4, -2.5, -1, 0, 2.5, 4, 6, 7, 10\\}$.\nThe total number of elements in the set is 12.\nThe solutions to the equation are $4$, $-9$, and $-2.5$.\nWe need to check which of these solutions are present in the given set.\n$4$ is in the set.\n$-9$ is not in the set.\n$-2.5$ is in the set.\n\nSo, the numbers in the set that are solutions to the equation are $4$ and $-2.5$. There are 2 such numbers.\nThe probability of selecting a number from the set that is a solution to the equation is the number of solutions in the set divided by the total number of elements in the set.\nProbability = (Number of solutions in the set) / (Total number of elements in the set)\nProbability = $2 / 12 = 1 / 6$\n\nNow we compare this probability with the given options:\nA. 1/12\nB. 1/6\nC. 1/4\nD. 1/3\nE. 1/2\n\nThe calculated probability is 1/6, which corresponds to option B.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
