    "global index": "MathQA_782",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: each of 3 investments has a 20 % of becoming worthless within a year of purchase , independently of what happens to the other two investments . if simone invests an equal sum k in each of these 3 investments on january 1 , the approximate chance that by the end of the year , she loses no more than 1 / 3 of her original investment is\n\nOptions: \nA. 90 %\nB. 80 %\nC. 70 %\nD. 60 %\nE. 40 %\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $p$ be the probability that an investment becomes worthless, so $p = 0.2$.\nLet $q$ be the probability that an investment does not become worthless, so $q = 1 - p = 0.8$.\nThere are 3 independent investments, each with an initial investment of $k$.\nThe total initial investment is $3k$.\nSimone loses no more than 1/3 of her original investment if the total loss is less than or equal to $(1/3) * 3k = k$.\n\nLet $X$ be the number of investments that become worthless. $X$ follows a binomial distribution with $n=3$ and $p=0.2$.\nThe possible values of $X$ are 0, 1, 2, 3.\n\nIf $X=0$, no investments become worthless. The loss is $0 * k = 0$. This is less than or equal to $k$.\nThe probability of this is $P(X=0) = \\binom{3}{0} (0.2)^0 (0.8)^3 = 1 * 1 * 0.512 = 0.512$.\n\nIf $X=1$, one investment becomes worthless. The loss is $1 * k = k$. This is less than or equal to $k$.\nThe probability of this is $P(X=1) = \\binom{3}{1} (0.2)^1 (0.8)^2 = 3 * 0.2 * 0.64 = 0.6 * 0.64 = 0.384$.\n\nIf $X=2$, two investments become worthless. The loss is $2 * k = 2k$. This is greater than $k$.\nThe probability of this is $P(X=2) = \\binom{3}{2} (0.2)^2 (0.8)^1 = 3 * 0.04 * 0.8 = 0.12 * 0.8 = 0.096$.\n\nIf $X=3$, all three investments become worthless. The loss is $3 * k = 3k$. This is greater than $k$.\nThe probability of this is $P(X=3) = \\binom{3}{3} (0.2)^3 (0.8)^0 = 1 * 0.008 * 1 = 0.008$.\n\nThe chance that she loses no more than 1/3 of her original investment is the probability that $X=0$ or $X=1$.\n$P(\\text{loss} \\le k) = P(X=0) + P(X=1) = 0.512 + 0.384 = 0.896$.\n\nThis is approximately 90%.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{A}$.",
      "success": true,
