    "global index": "MathQA_1413",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a metallic sheet is of rectangular shape with dimensions 48 m x 34 m . from each of its corners , a square is cut off so as to make an open box . if the length of the square is 8 m , the volume of the box ( in m 3 ) is :\n\nOptions: \nA. 4830\nB. 5120\nC. 4608\nD. 7500\nE. 8960\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the dimensions of the rectangular metallic sheet be $L = 48$ m and $W = 34$ m.\nSquares of side length $s = 8$ m are cut off from each of its corners.\n\nWhen squares of side length $s$ are cut off from each corner, the length of the base of the open box will be $L - 2s$ and the width of the base will be $W - 2s$. The height of the box will be $s$.\n\nLength of the base of the box = $48 - 2 \\times 8 = 48 - 16 = 32$ m.\nWidth of the base of the box = $34 - 2 \\times 8 = 34 - 16 = 18$ m.\nHeight of the box = $8$ m.\n\nThe volume of the box is given by the formula: Volume = Length × Width × Height.\nVolume = $(L - 2s) \\times (W - 2s) \\times s$\nVolume = $32 \\times 18 \\times 8$\n\nFirst, calculate $32 \\times 18$:\n$32 \\times 18 = 32 \\times (20 - 2) = 32 \\times 20 - 32 \\times 2 = 640 - 64 = 576$.\n\nNow, multiply the result by the height:\nVolume = $576 \\times 8$.\n$576 \\times 8 = (500 + 70 + 6) \\times 8 = 500 \\times 8 + 70 \\times 8 + 6 \\times 8 = 4000 + 560 + 48 = 4608$.\n\nThus, the volume of the box is $4608$ m$^3$.\n\nComparing this value with the given options:\nA. 4830\nB. 5120\nC. 4608\nD. 7500\nE. 8960\n\nThe calculated volume matches option C.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$.",
