    "global index": "MathQA_1769",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: on a ranch , a rancher can place a loop of rope , called a lasso , once in every 3 throws around a cow ’ s neck . what is the probability that the rancher will be able to place a lasso around a cow ’ s neck at least once in 3 attempts ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 / 3\nB. 5 / 9\nC. 7 / 9\nD. 19 / 27\nE. 23 / 27\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let P(success) be the probability of placing a lasso around a cow's neck in one throw.\nGiven P(success) = 1/3.\nLet P(failure) be the probability of not placing a lasso around a cow's neck in one throw.\nP(failure) = 1 - P(success) = 1 - 1/3 = 2/3.\n\nWe want to find the probability that the rancher will be able to place a lasso around a cow's neck at least once in 3 attempts.\nThis is equivalent to 1 - P(no success in 3 attempts).\nP(no success in 3 attempts) = P(failure in 1st attempt) * P(failure in 2nd attempt) * P(failure in 3rd attempt)\nSince each attempt is independent,\nP(no success in 3 attempts) = (2/3) * (2/3) * (2/3) = 8/27.\n\nThe probability of at least one success in 3 attempts = 1 - P(no success in 3 attempts)\n= 1 - 8/27\n= 27/27 - 8/27\n= 19/27.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 164,
        "output_tokens": 283,
