      "generated_answer": "The volume of a cube with edge length 's' is given by $s^3$.\nThe volumes of the three iron cubes are:\n$V_1 = (6 \\text{ cm})^3 = 216 \\text{ cm}^3$\n$V_2 = (8 \\text{ cm})^3 = 512 \\text{ cm}^3$\n$V_3 = (10 \\text{ cm})^3 = 1000 \\text{ cm}^3$\n\nWhen these three cubes are melted and formed into a single cube, the total volume remains the same.\nTotal volume, $V_{total} = V_1 + V_2 + V_3 = 216 + 512 + 1000 = 1728 \\text{ cm}^3$.\n\nLet the edge of the new single cube be 'a' cm.\nThe volume of the new cube is $a^3$.\nSo, $a^3 = 1728 \\text{ cm}^3$.\n\nTo find the edge length 'a', we need to find the cube root of 1728.\nWe can test the given options:\nA. $10^3 = 1000$\nB. $12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 144 \\times 12 = 1728$\nC. $16^3 = 16 \\times 16 \\times 16 = 256 \\times 16 = 4096$\nD. $18^3 = 18 \\times 18 \\times 18 = 324 \\times 18 = 5832$\n\nSince $12^3 = 1728$, the edge of the new cube formed is 12 cm.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
