      "generated_answer": "Let I be the monthly income of the labourer.\nFor the first 10 months, the average expenditure is 85. So, total expenditure in the first 10 months = $10 \\times 85 = 850$.\nDuring this period, he fell into debt. This means his expenditure was more than his income.\nLet the debt amount be D. So, $10 \\times I - 850 = -D \\Rightarrow 850 - 10I = D$.\n\nIn the next 4 months, he reduced his monthly expenses to 60. So, total expenditure in the next 4 months = $4 \\times 60 = 240$.\nIn these 4 months, he not only cleared off his debt but also saved 30.\nThis means that in these 4 months, his total income minus his total expenditure equals the debt cleared plus the savings.\nSo, $4 \\times I - 240 = D + 30$.\n\nNow we have two equations:\n1) $D = 850 - 10I$\n2) $D + 30 = 4I - 240$\n\nSubstitute the first equation into the second one:\n$(850 - 10I) + 30 = 4I - 240$\n$880 - 10I = 4I - 240$\n$880 + 240 = 4I + 10I$\n$1120 = 14I$\n$I = \\frac{1120}{14}$\n$I = 80$\n\nLet's check the answer.\nIf monthly income is 80.\nIn the first 10 months:\nTotal income = $10 \\times 80 = 800$.\nTotal expenditure = $10 \\times 85 = 850$.\nDebt = $850 - 800 = 50$.\n\nIn the next 4 months:\nTotal income = $4 \\times 80 = 320$.\nTotal expenditure = $4 \\times 60 = 240$.\nAmount saved/cleared = $320 - 240 = 80$.\nHe cleared the debt of 50 and saved 30. So, $50 + 30 = 80$. This matches.\n\nSo, his monthly income is 80.\nHowever, 80 is not among the given options. This suggests there might be an error in the question or the options provided, or my interpretation. Let me re-read the problem carefully.\n\nLet's re-evaluate.\nLet average monthly income be x.\nTotal income in 10 months = 10x\nTotal expenditure in 10 months = 10 * 85 = 850\nDebt = 850 - 10x  (Equation 1)\n\nTotal income in next 4 months = 4x\nTotal expenditure in next 4 months = 4 * 60 = 240\nAmount saved/cleared in next 4 months = 4x - 240\nThis amount is equal to the debt cleared plus 30 (savings).\nSo, 4x - 240 = Debt + 30  (Equation 2)\n\nSubstitute Equation 1 into Equation 2:\n4x - 240 = (850 - 10x) + 30\n4x - 240 = 880 - 10x\n4x + 10x = 880 + 240\n14x = 1120\nx = 1120 / 14\nx = 80\n\nThe calculated monthly income is 80. Since 80 is not an option, the correct answer is E.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$",
