d. The first prism exposes two triangular faces and three rectangular faces. When joined, one rectangular face disappears. So 2 triangles and 2 rectangles exposed from the first prism.\nThe second prism's triangular faces are internal. Two of its rectangular faces are exposed.\nThe third prism's two triangular faces are exposed. Its two outer rectangular faces are exposed.\nThis gives $2 + 2 + 2 + 2 = 8$ rectangular faces. Total $2 + 8 = 10$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
