    "global index": "MathQA_436",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a 12 meter long wire is cut into two pieces . if the longer piece is then used to form a perimeter of a square , what is the probability that the area of the square will be more than 4 if the original wire was cut at an arbitrary point ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 / 6\nB. 2 / 3\nC. 3 / 10\nD. 1 / 3\nE. 2 / 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the length of the wire be $L=12$ meters. The wire is cut into two pieces. Let the length of one piece be $x$ meters, where $0 < x < 12$. Then the length of the other piece is $12-x$ meters.\nThe longer piece is used to form the perimeter of a square.\nCase 1: The first piece of length $x$ is longer. So, $x > 12-x$, which means $2x > 12$, or $x > 6$. In this case, the perimeter of the square is $x$. The side length of the square is $\\frac{x}{4}$. The area of the square is $A = (\\frac{x}{4})^2 = \\frac{x^2}{16}$.\nWe want the area to be more than 4, so $A > 4$.\n$\\frac{x^2}{16} > 4$\n$x^2 > 64$\nSince $x > 0$, we have $x > 8$.\nSo, for this case, we need $6 < x < 12$ and $x > 8$. This means $8 < x < 12$.\n\nCase 2: The second piece of length $12-x$ is longer. So, $12-x > x$, which means $12 > 2x$, or $x < 6$. In this case, the perimeter of the square is $12-x$. The side length of the square is $\\frac{12-x}{4}$. The area of the square is $A = (\\frac{12-x}{4})^2 = \\frac{(12-x)^2}{16}$.\nWe want the area to be more than 4, so $A > 4$.\n$\\frac{(12-x)^2}{16} > 4$\n$(12-x)^2 > 64$\nTaking the square root of both sides, $|12-x| > 8$.\nThis means either $12-x > 8$ or $12-x < -8$.\nFor $12-x > 8$, we get $12-8 > x$, so $4 > x$.\nFor $12-x < -8$, we get $12+8 < x$, so $20 < x$.\nSo, for this case, we need $0 < x < 6$ and ($4 > x$ or $20 < x$). Since $x<6$, the condition $20<x$ is not possible. Thus, we need $0 < x < 4$.\n\nCombining both cases, the wire is cut at an arbitrary point, which means $x$ can be any value in the interval $(0, 12)$. The length of the interval is 12.\nThe conditions for the area of the square to be more than 4 are $8 < x < 12$ or $0 < x < 4$.\nThe total length of these intervals is $(12-8) + (4-0) = 4 + 4 = 8$.\nThe probability that the area of the square will be more than 4 is the ratio of the total favorable length to the total possible length.\nProbability = $\\frac{\\text{Favorable length}}{\\text{Total length}} = \\frac{8}{12} = \\frac{2}{3}$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
