    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a 14 meter long wire is cut into two pieces . if the longer piece is then used to form a perimeter of a square , what is the probability that the area of the square will be more than 4 if the original wire was cut at an arbitrary point ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5 / 14\nB. 3 / 14\nC. 8 / 21\nD. 6 / 7\nE. 2 / 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the length of the wire be $L = 14$ meters. The wire is cut into two pieces. Let the length of the first piece be $x$ and the length of the second piece be $14 - x$. Since the wire is cut at an arbitrary point, $x$ can be any value in the interval $(0, 14)$.\n\nThe longer piece is used to form a square. There are two cases for which piece is longer:\nCase 1: $x > 14 - x$, which means $2x > 14$, or $x > 7$. In this case, the longer piece has length $x$.\nCase 2: $14 - x > x$, which means $14 > 2x$, or $x < 7$. In this case, the longer piece has length $14 - x$.\n\nIf the longer piece has length $s$, then the perimeter of the square is $s$. The side of the square is $\\frac{s}{4}$. The area of the square is $(\\frac{s}{4})^2 = \\frac{s^2}{16}$.\n\nWe are given that the area of the square is more than 4. So, $\\frac{s^2}{16} > 4$, which implies $s^2 > 64$, or $s > 8$.\n\nNow let's consider the two cases:\nCase 1: $x > 7$. The longer piece has length $x$. We need $x > 8$. So, for this case, we are interested in the interval $(8, 14)$. The length of this interval is $14 - 8 = 6$.\nCase 2: $x < 7$. The longer piece has length $14 - x$. We need $14 - x > 8$, which implies $14 - 8 > x$, or $x < 6$. So, for this case, we are interested in the interval $(0, 6)$. The length of this interval is $6 - 0 = 6$.\n\nCombining both cases, the values of $x$ for which the area of the square is more than 4 are when $x \\in (0, 6)$ or $x \\in (8, 14)$. The total length of these intervals is $6 + 6 = 12$.\n\nSince the wire was cut at an arbitrary point, $x$ is uniformly distributed over the interval $(0, 14)$. The total possible length for $x$ is $14$.\nThe probability that the area of the square will be more than 4 is the ratio of the length of the favorable intervals to the total length of the possible interval for $x$.\n\nProbability = $\\frac{\\text{Length of favorable intervals}}{\\text{Total length of possible interval}} = \\frac{12}{14} = \\frac{6}{7}$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
