      "generated_answer": "To find the increase in surface area, first calculate the surface area of the original 5 cm cube, which is \\(6 \\times (5 \\text{ cm})^2 = 150 \\text{ cm}^2\\). The original cube is cut into \\(5^3 = 125\\) smaller 1 cm cubes, each with a surface area of \\(6 \\times (1 \\text{ cm})^2 = 6 \\text{ cm}^2\\), giving a total surface area of \\(125 \\times 6 = 750 \\text{ cm}^2\\). The increase in surface area is \\(750 - 150 = 600 \\text{ cm}^2\\), resulting in a percentage increase of \\(\\frac{600}{150} \\times 100\\% = 400\\%\\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).",
