    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10539",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the capacitance of a single, isolated conducting sphere of radius a.\n\nOptions: \nA. C = πε₀a\nB. C = 10πε₀a\nC. C = 2πε₀a\nD. C = 12πε₀a\nE. C = 6πε₀a\nF. C = 3πε₀a\nG. C = 7πε₀a\nH. C = 8πε₀a\nI. C = 4πε₀a\nJ. C = 5πε₀a\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The capacitance of an isolated conducting sphere of radius $a$ is given by the formula $C = 4\\pi\\epsilon_0 a$. This formula is derived by considering the electric potential on the surface of the sphere when it carries a charge $Q$. The electric field outside the sphere is that of a point charge, and integrating this field to find the potential relative to infinity yields $V = \\frac{Q}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0 a}$. By definition, capacitance is $C = \\frac{Q}{V}$, which when substituted gives $C = \\frac{Q}{\\frac{Q}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0 a}} = 4\\pi\\epsilon_0 a$.\n\nComparing this formula to the given options, we find it matches option I.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{I}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 176,
        "output_tokens": 172,
        "total_tokens": 348
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
