    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10885",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The resistance in the circuit of the moving coil of a dynamometer wattmeter should be\n\nOptions: \nA. Low.\nB. Very low.\nC. High.\nD. Almost zero.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Rethinking the question, it asks about the resistance in the moving coil of a dynamometer wattmeter. The moving coil in a dynamometer wattmeter carries current proportional to the voltage. To ensure accurate measurement and minimize the current drawn from the circuit, the resistance of the voltage (or potential) coil should be high.\n\nThe provided options are:\nA. Low.\nB. Very low.\nC. High.\nD. Almost zero.\n\nSince the moving coil acts as the potential coil in a dynamometer wattmeter, its resistance should be high to limit the current flowing through it and to prevent it from significantly affecting the circuit it's measuring.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$",
