  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10196",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A man is informed that, when a pair of dice were rolled, the resulting sum was a \"seven\". How much information is there in this message?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4 bits\nB. 1.5 bits\nC. 2.585 bits\nD. 1 bit\nE. 3.5 bits\nF. 1.75 bits\nG. 3 bits\nH. 2 bits\nI. 5 bits\nJ. 2.321 bits\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the amount of information, we need to calculate the entropy of the event, which is the amount of uncertainty reduced by the message. The formula for information content is $I = -\\log_2(P)$, where $P$ is the probability of the event.\n\nWhen rolling a pair of dice, there are $6 \\times 6 = 36$ possible outcomes. The sums range from 2 to 12. The number of ways to obtain a sum of 7 is: (1,6), (2,5), (3,4), (4,3), (5,2), (6,1). There are 6 ways to get a sum of 7.\n\nTherefore, the probability of rolling a sum of 7 is $P(\\text{sum}=7) = \\frac{6}{36} = \\frac{1}{6}$.\n\nThe amount of information is $I = -\\log_2(\\frac{1}{6})$.\n$I = -\\log_2(1) - \\log_2(6) = 0 - \\log_2(6)$\n$I = -\\log_2(6)$\n\nWe know that $\\log_2(6) = \\log_2(2 \\times 3) = \\log_2(2) + \\log_2(3) = 1 + \\log_2(3)$.\nUsing the approximation $\\log_2(3) \\approx 1.585$.\nSo, $I \\approx -(1 + 1.585) = -2.585$.\nSince information is typically represented as a positive value (representing the reduction in uncertainty), the information content is $I = \\log_2(6)$.\n\nLet's calculate $\\log_2(6)$ more precisely.\n$\\log_2(6) = \\frac{\\log_{10}(6)}{\\log_{10}(2)} = \\frac{0.77815}{0.30103} \\approx 2.585$.\n\nSo, the amount of information is approximately 2.585 bits.\n\nComparing this to the given options:\nA. 4 bits\nB. 1.5 bits\nC. 2.585 bits\nD. 1 bit\nE. 3.5 bits\nF. 1.75 bits\nG. 3 bits\nH. 2 bits\nI. 5 bits\nJ. 2.321 bits\n\nThe calculated value matches option C.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 168,
        "output_tokens": 560,
        "total_tokens": 728
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
