es 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 24$.\nSo the probability is $24 / 6,497,400$.\n$24 / 6,497,400 \\approx 0.0000036937$.\n\nLet's look at the options again and multiply our probability by them to see if we get close to 1.\nOur probability is approximately 0.00000369.\nLet's look at the options in decimal form:\nA. 0.000057\nB. 0.000037\nC. 0.000107\nD. 0.000077\nE. 0.000007\nF. 0.000097\nG. 0.000027\nH. 0.000047\nI. 0.000017\nJ. 0.000002\n\nOur calculated probability is approximately 0.00000369. Option E is 0.000007. This is roughly twice our calculated probability. Option J is 0.000002, which is roughly half our calculated probability.\n\nLet's re-evaluate our calculation.\nP(1st ace) = 4/52\nP(2nd ace | 1st ace) = 3/51\nP(3rd ace | 1st 2 aces) = 2/50\nP(4th ace | 1st 3 aces) = 1/49\nProbability = (4/52) * (3/51) * (2/50) * (1/49) = 24 / 6497400 = 0.0000036937\n\nLet's consider the possibility that one of the options is the result of a calculation error.\nLet's check if any of the options are close to 1/270725.\n1/270725 ≈ 0.0000036937. This is the probability of drawing the 4 aces in any order. The question asks for drawing them *as the first 4 cards*.\n\nLet's scale our probability by a factor of 2 to see if it matches any option.\n0.0000036937 * 2 = 0.0000073874. This is very close to option E (0.000007).\n\nIt is likely that the intended calculation leads to a value that matches one of the options more closely. Let's review the options provided. Given the options, it's possible there is a slight discrepancy or rounding involved in how the options were generated.\n\nLet's consider option E: 0.000007.\nIf the probability were 0.000007, what would the numerator/denominator have to be?\nOur calculated value is 24 / 6497400.\nIf we round 24 / 6497400 to some precision, we get 0.0000037.\n\nLet's re-examine the options and our calculation carefully.\nOur calculation: (4/52) * (3/51) * (2/50) * (1/49) = 24 / 6,497,400 ≈ 0.0000036937.\n\nLet's assume there's a typo in the options and one of them is meant to be closer.\nHowever, we must choose the best fit.\nComparing 0.0000036937 with the options:\nE. 0.000007\nJ. 0.000002\n\n0.000007 is closer to 0.0000036937 if we are looking for a value that's roughly twice our result. This would imply an error in the calculation of the options.\n\nLet's assume the question is correctly stated and the options are provided. We have calculated the precise probability. We need to find the closest option.\nLet's convert the difference between our result and each option:\n|0.0000036937 - 0.000007| = 0.0000033063\n|0.0000036937 - 0.000002| = 0.0000016937\n\nComparing the absolute differences, 0.0000016937 is smaller than 0.0000033063.\nTherefore, option J (0.000002) is closer to our calculated probability than option E (0.000007).\n\nRethinking the problem. The initial calculation of the probability is correct. The discrepancy is with the provided options. Based on the calculation, J is the closest option.\n\nFinal check:\nProbability = 24 / 6,497,400 = 0.0000036937...\nOption J = 0.000002\nDifference = 0.0000016937\n\nOption E = 0.000007\nDifference = 0.0000033063\n\nOption J is indeed closer.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{J}$.",
