    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10561",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compute the conditional distribution of Y given X if X and Y are jointly distributed with density f(x, y) = x + y0 < x < 1, 0 < y < 1 and = 0otherwise. What is the conditional expectation of Y?\n\nOptions: \nA. (x + 2) / {{2(x + 1)}}\nB. (2x + 3) / {{2(3x + 1)}}\nC. (2x + 2) / {{4(2x + 1)}}\nD. (3x + 3) / {{3(3x + 2)}}\nE. (2x + 1) / {{3(x + 2)}}\nF. (x + 1) / {{2(2x + 1)}}\nG. (3x + 2) / {{3(2x + 1)}}\nH. (3x + 1) / {{3(2x + 2)}}\nI. (4x + 2) / {{4(3x + 1)}}\nJ. (3x + 2) / {{4(2x + 1)}}\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To compute the conditional distribution of Y given X, we first need the marginal distribution of X.\nThe marginal density of X is given by $f\\_X(x) = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} f(x, y) dy$.\nFor $0 < x < 1$, $f\\_X(x) = \\int_{0}^{1} (x + y) dy = [xy + y^2/2]_0^1 = x + 1/2$.\nThe conditional density of Y given X is $f\\_{Y|X}(y|x) = f(x, y) / f\\_X(x) = (x + y) / (x + 1/2)$.\nFor $0 < y < 1$, $f\\_{Y|X}(y|x) = (2x + 2y) / (2x + 1)$.\n\nThe conditional expectation of Y given X is $E[Y|X=x] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y f\\_{Y|X}(y|x) dy$.\nFor $0 < x < 1$, $E[Y|X=x] = \\int_{0}^{1} y \\frac{2x + 2y}{2x + 1} dy = \\frac{1}{2x + 1} \\int_{0}^{1} (2xy + 2y^2) dy$.\n$E[Y|X=x] = \\frac{1}{2x + 1} [xy^2 + \\frac{2}{3}y^3]_0^1 = \\frac{1}{2x + 1} (x + \\frac{2}{3}) = \\frac{3x + 2}{3(2x + 1)}$.\n\nComparing this result with the given options, we see that option G matches: (3x + 2) / {{3(2x + 1)}}.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{G}$.",
