      "generated_answer": "To compute the expected value E(X), we use the formula E(X) = $\\sum x_i * Pr(X = x_i)$.\nE(X) = $(0 * 8/27) + (1 * 12/27) + (2 * 6/27) + (3 * 1/27)$ = $0 + 12/27 + 12/27 + 3/27$ = $27/27$ = 1.\n\nTo compute the variance Var(X), we use the formula Var(X) = E(X^2) - [E(X)]^2.\nFirst, we compute E(X^2) = $\\sum x_i^2 * Pr(X = x_i)$.\nE(X^2) = $(0^2 * 8/27) + (1^2 * 12/27) + (2^2 * 6/27) + (3^2 * 1/27)$ = $(0 * 8/27) + (1 * 12/27) + (4 * 6/27) + (9 * 1/27)$ = $0 + 12/27 + 24/27 + 9/27$ = $45/27$ = $5/3$.\nNow, Var(X) = E(X^2) - [E(X)]^2 = $5/3 - (1)^2$ = $5/3 - 1$ = $2/3$.\n\nTherefore, E(X) = 1 and Var(X) = 2/3.\n\nComparing this to the options:\nA. E(X) = 3/2, Var(X) = 1/4\nB. E(X) = 2, Var(X) = 1/3\nC. E(X) = 5/3, Var(X) = 5/9\nD. E(X) = 1, Var(X) = 2/3\nE. E(X) = 3/4, Var(X) = 3/8\nF. E(X) = 2/3, Var(X) = 1\nG. E(X) = 0.5, Var(X) = 0.5\nH. E(X) = 1.5, Var(X) = 1.5\nI. E(X) = 1/2, Var(X) = 1/2\nJ. E(X) = 1/3, Var(X) = 2\n\nThe correct option is D.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
