      "generated_answer": "The given Fourier series is in exponential form: $f(t) = \\sum_{k=-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{1+jk} e^{jkt}$.\nTo convert this to trigonometric form, we need to consider the cases for $k=0$ and $k \\neq 0$.\n\nFor $k=0$: The term is $\\frac{1}{1+j(0)} e^{j(0)t} = 1$. This corresponds to the DC component (constant term) of the trigonometric Fourier series.\n\nFor $k \\neq 0$: We can write $e^{jkt} = \\cos(kt) + j\\sin(kt)$.\nSo, the terms for $k \\neq 0$ are:\n$\\frac{1}{1+jk} e^{jkt} = \\frac{1}{1+jk} (\\cos(kt) + j\\sin(kt))$\nTo simplify, multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n$= \\frac{1}{1+jk} \\times \\frac{1-jk}{1-jk} (\\cos(kt) + j\\sin(kt))$\n$= \\frac{1-jk}{1 - (jk)^2} (\\cos(kt) + j\\sin(kt))$\n$= \\frac{1-jk}{1 + k^2} (\\cos(kt) + j\\sin(kt))$\n$= \\frac{1}{1+k^2} (1-jk)(\\cos(kt) + j\\sin(kt))$\n$= \\frac{1}{1+k^2} [\\cos(kt) + j\\sin(kt) - jk\\cos(kt) - j^2k\\sin(kt)]$\n$= \\frac{1}{1+k^2} [\\cos(kt) + j\\sin(kt) - jk\\cos(kt) + k\\sin(kt)]$\n$= \\frac{1}{1+k^2} [(\\cos(kt) + k\\sin(kt)) + j(\\sin(kt) - k\\cos(kt))]$\n\nThe Fourier series is $f(t) = c_0 + \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} (c_k e^{jkt} + c_{-k} e^{-jkt})$.\nIn our case, the coefficients are $c_k = \\frac{1}{1+jk}$.\nThen $c_{-k} = \\frac{1}{1+j(-k)} = \\frac{1}{1-jk}$.\nWe know that $c_k = a_k + jb_k$ and $c_{-k} = a_k - jb_k$.\nFrom the expansion of $c_k e^{jkt}$, the real part is $\\frac{1}{1+k^2}(\\cos(kt) + k\\sin(kt))$ and the imaginary part is $\\frac{1}{1+k^2}(\\sin(kt) - k\\cos(kt))$.\n\nFor the trigonometric form, $f(t) = a_0 + \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} (a_k \\cos(kt) + b_k \\sin(kt))$.\nWe have $a_0 = c_0 = 1$.\nFor $k \\neq 0$, the terms in the summation are:\n$c_k e^{jkt} + c_{-k} e^{-jkt} = 2 \\text{Re}(c_k e^{jkt})$.\nSo, $2 \\text{Re}(c_k e^{jkt}) = 2 \\times \\frac{1}{1+k^2}(\\cos(kt) + k\\sin(kt)) = \\frac{2(\\cos(kt) + k\\sin(kt))}{1+k^2}$.\n\nTherefore, the trigonometric form is $f(t) = 1 + \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{2(\\cos(kt) + k\\sin(kt))}{1+k^2}$.\n\nComparing this with the given options:\nOption D matches this form.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
