      "generated_answer": "To find the determinant of the 2x2 matrix \\( A = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\end{pmatrix} \\), we use the formula for the determinant of a 2x2 matrix, which is \\( ad - bc \\). Here, \\( a = 2 \\), \\( b = 3 \\), \\( c = 1 \\), and \\( d = 2 \\). Therefore, the determinant is \\( (2)(2) - (3)(1) = 4 - 3 = 1 \\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).",
