    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10349",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If six messages having probabilities (1 / 4), (1 / 4), (1 / 8), (1 / 8), (1 / 8) and (1 / 8) can be accommodated in a single communication system, determine the entropy.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.00 bits/message\nB. 2.25 bits/message\nC. 1.75 bits/message\nD. 3.00 bits/message\nE. 2.75 bits/message\nF. 3.25 bits/message\nG. 4.00 bits/message\nH. 3.50 bits/message\nI. 2.50 bits/message\nJ. 1.50 bits/message\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The entropy H of a discrete random variable X with possible values $x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_n$ and their corresponding probabilities $p(x_1), p(x_2), \\dots, p(x_n)$ is given by the formula:\n$$H(X) = -\\sum_{i=1}^{n} p(x_i) \\log_2 p(x_i)$$\n\nIn this problem, we have six messages with the following probabilities:\n$p_1 = 1/4$\n$p_2 = 1/4$\n$p_3 = 1/8$\n$p_4 = 1/8$\n$p_5 = 1/8$\n$p_6 = 1/8$\n\nNow, we calculate the entropy using the formula:\n$H = -(p_1 \\log_2 p_1 + p_2 \\log_2 p_2 + p_3 \\log_2 p_3 + p_4 \\log_2 p_4 + p_5 \\log_2 p_5 + p_6 \\log_2 p_6)$\n$H = -[(1/4) \\log_2 (1/4) + (1/4) \\log_2 (1/4) + (1/8) \\log_2 (1/8) + (1/8) \\log_2 (1/8) + (1/8) \\log_2 (1/8) + (1/8) \\log_2 (1/8)]$\nWe know that $\\log_2 (1/4) = \\log_2 (2^{-2}) = -2$ and $\\log_2 (1/8) = \\log_2 (2^{-3}) = -3$.\n$H = -[2 \\times (1/4) \\times (-2) + 4 \\times (1/8) \\times (-3)]$\n$H = -[2 \\times (-1/2) + 4 \\times (-3/8)]$\n$H = -[-1 + (-12/8)]$\n$H = -[-1 - 3/2]$\n$H = -[-5/2]$\n$H = 5/2$\n$H = 2.5$ bits/message\n\nComparing this value with the given options:\nA. 2.00 bits/message\nB. 2.25 bits/message\nC. 1.75 bits/message\nD. 3.00 bits/message\nE. 2.75 bits/message\nF. 3.25 bits/message\nG. 4.00 bits/message\nH. 3.50 bits/message\nI. 2.50 bits/message\nJ. 1.50 bits/message\n\nThe calculated entropy is 2.50 bits/message, which corresponds to option I.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{I}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 227,
        "output_tokens": 665,
