  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10660",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 0 - 100 V voltmeter has a guaranteed accuracy of 2 % of full scale reading. The voltage measured by the voltmeter is 75 V. The limiting error is in percentage\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 %.\nB. 2.66 %.\nC. 2.5 %.\nD. 5 %.\nE. 2 %.\nF. 1.5 %.\nG. 2.33 %.\nH. 3.33 %.\nI. 3 %.\nJ. 4 %.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The limiting error is calculated as the percentage of the full-scale reading.\nGiven that the full-scale reading is 100 V and the accuracy is 2% of the full-scale reading, the absolute error is 2% of 100 V, which is 2 V.\nThe percentage error for the measured value of 75 V is then (2 V / 75 V) * 100%.\n\nCalculation:\nAbsolute error = 2% of full scale = 0.02 * 100 V = 2 V.\nPercentage error = (Absolute error / Measured value) * 100%\nPercentage error = (2 V / 75 V) * 100% = (2/75) * 100% = 200/75 % = 8/15 * 100% = 800/15 % = 160/3 % = 53.33...%\n\nLet re-read the question carefully. \"The limiting error is in percentage\". The question is asking for the percentage error of the reading.\nThe accuracy is given as \"2 % of full scale reading\". This means the maximum deviation from the true value is 2% of the full scale.\n\nLet's recalculate using the correct interpretation of \"limiting error\" in this context.\nThe accuracy statement \"2% of full scale reading\" defines the maximum possible absolute error, irrespective of the measured value.\nSo, the maximum absolute error = 2% of 100 V = 0.02 * 100 V = 2 V.\n\nWhen the voltmeter reads 75 V, the actual voltage could be anywhere between 75 V - 2 V (73 V) and 75 V + 2 V (77 V).\nThe limiting error as a percentage of the *reading* is calculated as:\nLimiting error % = (Maximum absolute error / Measured reading) * 100%\nLimiting error % = (2 V / 75 V) * 100%\n\nLimiting error % = (2/75) * 100 = 200/75 = 8/3 = 2.666... %\n\nLooking at the options, 2.66% is the closest to this calculation.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 176,
        "output_tokens": 527,
        "total_tokens": 703
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
