    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10173",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the inverse Laplace transform of F(s) = [(2s^2 - 4) / {{(s - 2)(s + 1)(s - 3)}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. f(t) = [(- 4) / 3]e^-2t - (1 / 6)e^2t + (7 / 2)e^-3t\nB. f(t) = [(- 4) / 3]e^2t - (1 / 6)e^-t - (7 / 2)e^3t\nC. f(t) = [(- 4) / 3]e^3t - (1 / 6)e^2t + (7 / 2)e^-t\nD. f(t) = [(- 4) / 3]e^-2t - (1 / 6)e^t - (7 / 2)e^3t\nE. f(t) = [(- 4) / 3]e^2t + (1 / 6)e^t - (7 / 2)e^3t\nF. f(t) = [(- 4) / 3]e^2t - (1 / 6)e^-t + (7 / 2)e^3t\nG. f(t) = 4e^2t - (1 / 3)e^-t + (7 / 6)e^3t\nH. f(t) = [(- 4) / 3]e^2t - (1 / 6)e^t + (7 / 2)e^3t\nI. f(t) = [(- 4) / 3]e^2t + (1 / 6)e^-t + (7 / 2)e^3t\nJ. f(t) = (4 / 3)e^2t + (1 / 6)e^-t - (7 / 2)e^3t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the inverse Laplace transform, we first perform a partial fraction decomposition of $F(s)$.\nLet $F(s) = \\frac{2s^2 - 4}{(s - 2)(s + 1)(s - 3)} = \\frac{A}{s - 2} + \\frac{B}{s + 1} + \\frac{C}{s - 3}$.\nMultiplying both sides by $(s - 2)(s + 1)(s - 3)$, we get $2s^2 - 4 = A(s + 1)(s - 3) + B(s - 2)(s - 3) + C(s - 2)(s + 1)$.\nSetting $s = 2$: $2(2)^2 - 4 = A(2 + 1)(2 - 3) \\Rightarrow 8 - 4 = A(3)(-1) \\Rightarrow 4 = -3A \\Rightarrow A = -\\frac{4}{3}$.\nSetting $s = -1$: $2(-1)^2 - 4 = B(-1 - 2)(-1 - 3) \\Rightarrow 2 - 4 = B(-3)(-4) \\Rightarrow -2 = 12B \\Rightarrow B = -\\frac{2}{12} = -\\frac{1}{6}$.\nSetting $s = 3$: $2(3)^2 - 4 = C(3 - 2)(3 + 1) \\Rightarrow 18 - 4 = C(1)(4) \\Rightarrow 14 = 4C \\Rightarrow C = \\frac{14}{4} = \\frac{7}{2}$.\nSo, $F(s) = -\\frac{4}{3}\\frac{1}{s - 2} - \\frac{1}{6}\\frac{1}{s + 1} + \\frac{7}{2}\\frac{1}{s - 3}$.\nThe inverse Laplace transform is $f(t) = \\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\{F(s)\\} = -\\frac{4}{3}e^{2t} - \\frac{1}{6}e^{-t} + \\frac{7}{2}e^{3t}$.\n\nComparing this with the given options, we find that it matches option F.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{F}$.",
      "success": true,
