  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10271",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An SCR has half cycle surge current rating of 3000 A for 50 Hz supply. One cycle surge current will be\n\nOptions: \nA. 2121.32 A.\nB. 6000 A.\nC. 2000 A.\nD. 7000 A.\nE. 5000 A.\nF. 3500 A.\nG. 1500 A.\nH. 4242.64 A.\nI. 3000 A.\nJ. 2500 A.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The surge current rating of a semiconductor device is often specified for a half-cycle duration. For a full cycle surge, the peak current would generally be lower than simple doubling of the half-cycle rating due to the thermal time constant of the device. A common approximation for the ratio of one-cycle surge current to half-cycle surge current for SCRs is approximately $\\sqrt{2}$. Thus, the one-cycle surge current would be roughly $3000 A \\times \\sqrt{2} \\approx 4242.64 A$.\n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{H}.",
