    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the inverse Laplace transform L^-1[1 / {{s(s^2 + 4)}}], using the convolution.\n\nOptions: \nA. (1 / 2)(e^(2t) - 1)\nB. (1 / 2)(1 + cos2t)\nC. (1 / 4)(1 - cos2t)\nD. (1 / 4)(sin(2t) - cos(2t))\nE. (1 / 2)sin(2t)\nF. e^(-2t) * sin(2t)\nG. (1 / 2)(1 - cos2t)\nH. t * sin(2t)\nI. (1 / 4)(1 + cos2t)\nJ. sin(2t)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "openai/gpt-4o-mini",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the inverse Laplace transform of \\( \\frac{1}{s(s^2 + 4)} \\) using the convolution theorem, we can express \\( \\frac{1}{s} \\) and \\( \\frac{1}{s^2 + 4} \\) separately. The inverse Laplace transforms are \\( L^{-1}\\left[\\frac{1}{s}\\right] = 1 \\) and \\( L^{-1}\\left[\\frac{1}{s^2 + 4}\\right] = \\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2t) \\). Using convolution gives \\( t * \\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2t) = \\frac{1}{2}(1 - \\cos(2t)) \\), leading us to choice G.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).",
