  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10560",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine the mean-square quantization error during the quantization of a signal. Assume that the error (equally likely) lies in the range - S/2 to + S/2, where S is the step size.\n\nOptions: \nA. (S^2 / 3)\nB. (S^2 / 12)\nC. (S^2 / 24)\nD. (S^2 / 8)\nE. (S^2 / 18)\nF. (S^2 / 10)\nG. (S^2 / 6)\nH. (S^2 / 30)\nI. (S^2 / 4)\nJ. (S^2 / 16)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The mean-square quantization error is the expected value of the square of the quantization error. Given that the error is equally likely to lie in the range $-S/2$ to $+S/2$, it follows a uniform distribution. The probability density function (PDF) for a uniform distribution over $[a, b]$ is $f(x) = \\frac{1}{b-a}$ for $a \\le x \\le b$, and 0 otherwise. In this case, $a = -S/2$ and $b = S/2$. So, the PDF is $f(e) = \\frac{1}{S/2 - (-S/2)} = \\frac{1}{S}$ for $-S/2 \\le e \\le S/2$.\n\nThe mean-square error is defined as $E[e^2] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} e^2 f(e) de$. For our problem, this becomes:\n$E[e^2] = \\int_{-S/2}^{S/2} e^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{S}\\right) de$\n$E[e^2] = \\frac{1}{S} \\int_{-S/2}^{S/2} e^2 de$\n$E[e^2] = \\frac{1}{S} \\left[\\frac{e^3}{3}\\right]_{-S/2}^{S/2}$\n$E[e^2] = \\frac{1}{S} \\left(\\frac{(S/2)^3}{3} - \\frac{(-S/2)^3}{3}\\right)$\n$E[e^2] = \\frac{1}{S} \\left(\\frac{S^3/8}{3} - \\frac{-S^3/8}{3}\\right)$\n$E[e^2] = \\frac{1}{S} \\left(\\frac{S^3}{24} + \\frac{S^3}{24}\\right)$\n$E[e^2] = \\frac{1}{S} \\left(\\frac{2S^3}{24}\\right)$\n$E[e^2] = \\frac{1}{S} \\left(\\frac{S^3}{12}\\right)$\n$E[e^2] = \\frac{S^2}{12}$\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 222,
        "output_tokens": 525,
        "total_tokens": 747
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
