  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10566",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the inverse Laplace transform L^-1 {{1 / (s - 1)^2}}, using the convolution.\n\nOptions: \nA. t^2e^t\nB. t e^2t\nC. e^(-t)\nD. t^3e^t\nE. te^t\nF. t^2e^(-t)\nG. e^t\nH. e^t * cos(t)\nI. e^2t\nJ. e^t * sin(t)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The question asks for the inverse Laplace transform of $1 / (s - 1)^2$ using convolution. We know that the Laplace transform of $t^n e^{at}$ is $n! / (s - a)^{n+1}$. In this case, we have $1 / (s - 1)^2$, which can be written as $1! / (s - 1)^{1+1}$. Comparing this to the general formula, we can see that $n = 1$ and $a = 1$. Therefore, the inverse Laplace transform is $t^1 e^{1t} = t e^t$.\n\nThe answer corresponds to option E.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
