  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10311",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Evaluate f(t) if F(s) = [(3s^2 + 17s + 47) / {{(s + 2)(s^2 + 4s + 29)}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. f(t) = [e^-2t + 2.24e^-2tsin(5t - 26.6°)] u(t)\nB. f(t) = [e^-2t + 2.24e^-2tcos(5t - 26.6°)] u(t)\nC. f(t) = [e^-2t - 2.24e^-2tcos(5t - 26.6°)] u(t)\nD. f(t) = [e^-2t + 2.24e^-2tcos(5t + 26.6°)] u(t)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "openai/gpt-4o-mini",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find \\( f(t) \\), we need to perform an inverse Laplace transform of \\( F(s) \\). The denominator indicates a combination of an exponential decay and a sinusoidal response, which typically results in terms involving both sine and cosine functions along with an exponential envelope. \n\nGiven the structure of the options, the presence of \\( e^{-2t} \\) strongly suggests that we have a shift due to the pole at \\( s = -2 \\), and the sinusoidal terms combined with \\( e^{-2t} \\) hint at resonance conditions—leading to a phase shift of \\( -26.6° \\). \n\nThus, the most fitting choice, considering these elements, is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{A}\\)",
      "success": true,
