    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10584",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A long wire composed of a smooth round conductor runs above and parallel to the ground (assumed to be a large conducting plane). A high voltage exists between the conductor and the ground. The maximum electric stress occurs at\n\nOptions: \nA. the point farthest from the ground on the conductor's surface.\nB. lower surface of the conductor.\nC. upper surface of the conductor.\nD. the midpoint of the conductor's surface.\nE. the point where the conductor and ground surface meet.\nF. the ground surface.\nG. midway between the conductor and ground.\nH. the point of the conductor farthest from the ground surface.\nI. the point closest to the ground on the conductor's surface.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
