  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10533",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use the sum of the steady-state and homogeneous solutions to find a sequence y [n] such that y [n] - (5/6)y [n - 1] + (1/6)y [n - 2] = 2, y [- 1] = 1, and y [-2] = - 7.\n\nOptions: \nA. 6 - (1/2)^n + (1/3)^n\nB. 6 - (1/2)^n - (1/3)^n\nC. 6 - (1/4)^n + (1/6)^n\nD. 6 + (1/2)^n - (1/3)^n\nE. 6 - (2/3)^n - (3/2)^n\nF. 6 + (1/2)^n + (1/3)^n\nG. 12 - (1/2)^n - (1/3)^n\nH. 6 + (1/2)^n + (2/3)^n\nI. 6 + 2^n - 3^n\nJ. 6 + (1/5)^n - (1/7)^n\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given difference equation is $y[n] - (5/6)y[n-1] + (1/6)y[n-2] = 2$.\nThe steady-state solution is a constant $y_p$. Substituting into the equation, we get $y_p - (5/6)y_p + (1/6)y_p = 2$, which simplifies to $(1 - 5/6 + 1/6)y_p = 2$, so $(2/6)y_p = 2$, which gives $y_p = 6$.\nThe characteristic equation for the homogeneous part $y_h[n] - (5/6)y_h[n-1] + (1/6)y_h[n-2] = 0$ is $r^2 - (5/6)r + (1/6) = 0$. Multiplying by 6, we get $6r^2 - 5r + 1 = 0$. Factoring this, we have $(3r - 1)(2r - 1) = 0$, so the roots are $r_1 = 1/3$ and $r_2 = 1/2$.\nThe homogeneous solution is of the form $y_h[n] = A(1/2)^n + B(1/3)^n$.\nThe total solution is $y[n] = y_p + y_h[n] = 6 + A(1/2)^n + B(1/3)^n$.\nWe are given initial conditions $y[-1] = 1$ and $y[-2] = -7$.\nFor $n = -1$, $y[-1] = 6 + A(1/2)^{-1} + B(1/3)^{-1} = 6 + 2A + 3B = 1$. So, $2A + 3B = -5$.\nFor $n = -2$, $y[-2] = 6 + A(1/2)^{-2} + B(1/3)^{-2} = 6 + 4A + 9B = -7$. So, $4A + 9B = -13$.\nWe have a system of two linear equations with two variables:\n1) $2A + 3B = -5$\n2) $4A + 9B = -13$\nMultiply equation (1) by 2: $4A + 6B = -10$.\nSubtract this from equation (2): $(4A + 9B) - (4A + 6B) = -13 - (-10)$, which gives $3B = -3$, so $B = -1$.\nSubstitute $B = -1$ into equation (1): $2A + 3(-1) = -5$, so $2A - 3 = -5$, which gives $2A = -2$, so $A = -1$.\nThus, the solution is $y[n] = 6 - (1/2)^n - (1/3)^n$.\n\nComparing with the options, option B matches our result.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
