  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10939",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given the Laplace transform of i(t), L[i(t)] = I(s) = [{{E - V(0^+)}} / {{R(s + (1 / RC))}}] Determine i(0^+).\n\nOptions: \nA. [{{E / (v(0^+) * R)}}]\nB. [{{v(0^+) - E}} / R]\nC. [{{E * v(0^+)}} / R]\nD. [{{E - v(0^+)}} * R]\nE. [{{E * R}} / {{v(0^+) - 1}}]\nF. [{{E + R}} / {{v(0^+) + RC}}]\nG. [{{(E - v(0^+)) / (R + RC)}}]\nH. [{{E + v(0^+)}} / R]\nI. [{{E * (v(0^+) + 1)}} / R]\nJ. [{{E - v(0^+)}} / R]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given Laplace transform is $I(s) = \\frac{E - V(0^+)}{R(s + \\frac{1}{RC})}$.\nWe know that the inverse Laplace transform of a function $F(s)$ can be related to the initial value of the time-domain function $f(t)$ using the initial value theorem, which states that $f(0^+) = \\lim_{s \\to \\infty} sF(s)$.\nIn this case, we have $I(s)$ instead of $F(s)$, and we want to find $i(0^+)$, which is the initial value of $i(t)$.\nApplying the initial value theorem, we have:\n$i(0^+) = \\lim_{s \\to \\infty} sI(s)$\n$i(0^+) = \\lim_{s \\to \\infty} s \\left[ \\frac{E - V(0^+)}{R(s + \\frac{1}{RC})} \\right]$\n$i(0^+) = \\lim_{s \\to \\infty} \\frac{s(E - V(0^+))}{R(s + \\frac{1}{RC})}$\nTo evaluate this limit, we can divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $s$ in the denominator, which is $s$:\n$i(0^+) = \\lim_{s \\to \\infty} \\frac{(E - V(0^+))}{R(1 + \\frac{1}{RCS})}$\nAs $s \\to \\infty$, the term $\\frac{1}{RCS}$ approaches 0.\nSo, the limit becomes:\n$i(0^+) = \\frac{E - V(0^+)}{R(1 + 0)}$\n$i(0^+) = \\frac{E - V(0^+)}{R}$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\frac{E - v(0^+)}{R}$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{J}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 290,
        "output_tokens": 430,
        "total_tokens": 720
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
