  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10562",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a factory four machines produce the same product. Machine A produces 10% of the output, machine B, 20%, machine C, 30%, and machine D, 40%. The proportion of defective items produced by these follows: Machine A: .001; Machine B: .0005; Machine C: .005; Machine D: .002. An item selected at random is found to be defective. What is the probability that the item was produced by A? by B? by C? by D?\n\nOptions: \nA. P(M_1|M) = 1/30, P(M_2|M) = 2/30, P(M_3|M) = 1/3, P(M_4|M) = 1/30\nB. P(M_1|M) = 1/15, P(M_2|M) = 1/15, P(M_3|M) = 1/2, P(M_4|M) = 2/15\nC. P(M_1|M) = 1/25, P(M_2|M) = 3/25, P(M_3|M) = 1/5, P(M_4|M) = 5/25\nD. P(M_1|M) = 2/25, P(M_2|M) = 2/25, P(M_3|M) = 1/4, P(M_4|M) = 7/25\nE. P(M_1|M) = 1/25, P(M_2|M) = 1/25, P(M_3|M) = 3/5, P(M_4|M) = 8/25\nF. P(M_1|M) = 1/25, P(M_2|M) = 1/25, P(M_3|M) = 1/5, P(M_4|M) = 1/25\nG. P(M_1|M) = 1/20, P(M_2|M) = 1/20, P(M_3|M) = 2/5, P(M_4|M) = 1/20\nH. P(M_1|M) = 1/50, P(M_2|M) = 1/50, P(M_3|M) = 1/10, P(M_4|M) = 1/50\nI. P(M_1|M) = 2/25, P(M_2|M) = 1/25, P(M_3|M) = 2/5, P(M_4|M) = 6/25\nJ. P(M_1|M) = 3/25, P(M_2|M) = 1/50, P(M_3|M) = 3/10, P(M_4|M) = 9/25\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "This is a classic application of Bayes' Theorem. We need to calculate the probability that an item came from a specific machine given that it is defective.\n\nLet:\n$P(A)$, $P(B)$, $P(C)$, $P(D)$ be the probabilities that an item comes from machine A, B, C, or D respectively.\n$P(D_A)$, $P(D_B)$, $P(D_C)$, $P(D_D)$ be the probabilities of an item being defective given it came from machine A, B, C, or D respectively.\n$P(M)$ be the probability that a randomly selected item is defective.\n\nGiven:\n$P(A) = 0.10$\n$P(B) = 0.20$\n$P(C) = 0.30$\n$P(D) = 0.40$\n\n$P(D_A) = 0.001$\n$P(D_B) = 0.0005$\n$P(D_C) = 0.005$\n$P(D_D) = 0.002$\n\nFirst, calculate the overall probability of a defective item, $P(M)$:\n$P(M) = P(D_A)P(A) + P(D_B)P(B) + P(D_C)P(C) + P(D_D)P(D)$\n$P(M) = (0.001)(0.10) + (0.0005)(0.20) + (0.005)(0.30) + (0.002)(0.40)$\n$P(M) = 0.0001 + 0.0001 + 0.0015 + 0.0008$\n$P(M) = 0.0025$\n\nNow, use Bayes' Theorem to find the probability that the item was produced by each machine given it is defective:\n$P(A|M) = \\frac{P(D_A)P(A)}{P(M)} = \\frac{(0.001)(0.10)}{0.0025} = \\frac{0.0001}{0.0025} = \\frac{1}{25}$\n$P(B|M) = \\frac{P(D_B)P(B)}{P(M)} = \\frac{(0.0005)(0.20)}{0.0025} = \\frac{0.0001}{0.0025} = \\frac{1}{25}$\n$P(C|M) = \\frac{P(D_C)P(C)}{P(M)} = \\frac{(0.005)(0.30)}{0.0025} = \\frac{0.0015}{0.0025} = \\frac{15}{25} = \\frac{3}{5}$\n$P(D|M) = \\frac{P(D_D)P(D)}{P(M)} = \\frac{(0.002)(0.40)}{0.0025} = \\frac{0.0008}{0.0025} = \\frac{8}{25}$\n\nComparing these probabilities with the given options, we find:\n$P(M_1|M) = 1/25$\n$P(M_2|M) = 1/25$\n$P(M_3|M) = 3/5$\n$P(M_4|M) = 8/25$\n\nThis matches option E.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$",
      "success": true,
