    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A Lissajous pattern on an oscilloscope has 5 horinzontal tangencies and 2 vertical tangencies. The frequency of horizontal input is 100 Hz. The frequency of the vertical will be\n\nOptions: \nA. 750 Hz.\nB. 250 Hz.\nC. 625 Hz.\nD. 500 Hz.\nE. 800 Hz.\nF. 400 Hz.\nG. 200 Hz.\nH. 900 Hz.\nI. 350 Hz.\nJ. 150 Hz.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The ratio of frequencies of the horizontal and vertical inputs to a Lissajous pattern is equal to the ratio of the number of vertical tangencies to the number of horizontal tangencies.\nHence, f_horizontal / f_vertical = number of vertical tangencies / number of horizontal tangencies.\nGiven that the number of horizontal tangencies is 5 and the number of vertical tangencies is 2, and the horizontal frequency is 100 Hz.\nTherefore, 100 Hz / f_vertical = 2 / 5.\nf_vertical = (100 Hz * 5) / 2 = 250 Hz.\n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{B}.",
