    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10016",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What inductance is required to resonate at 10 MHz with a capacitance of 100 pF?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.00 μH\nB. 1.53 μH\nC. 3.14 μH\nD. 3.53 μH\nE. 0.75 μH\nF. 2.00 μH\nG. 5.00 μH\nH. 4.00 μH\nI. 1.77 μH\nJ. 2.53 μH\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The resonant frequency ($f_r$) of an LC circuit is given by the formula:\n$f_r = \\frac{1}{2\\pi\\sqrt{LC}}$\n\nWe are given:\n$f_r$ = 10 MHz = $10 \\times 10^6$ Hz\n$C$ = 100 pF = $100 \\times 10^{-12}$ F\n\nWe need to find the inductance $L$. We can rearrange the formula to solve for $L$:\nSquaring both sides:\n$f_r^2 = \\frac{1}{4\\pi^2 LC}$\n$L = \\frac{1}{4\\pi^2 f_r^2 C}$\n\nNow, plug in the given values:\n$L = \\frac{1}{4\\pi^2 (10 \\times 10^6 \\text{ Hz})^2 (100 \\times 10^{-12} \\text{ F})}$\n$L = \\frac{1}{4\\pi^2 (100 \\times 10^{12}) (100 \\times 10^{-12})}$\n$L = \\frac{1}{4\\pi^2 (100 \\times 100)}$\n$L = \\frac{1}{4\\pi^2 (10000)}$\n$L = \\frac{1}{40000\\pi^2}$\n\nCalculate the value of $40000\\pi^2$:\n$\\pi^2 \\approx 9.8696$\n$40000 \\times 9.8696 \\approx 394784$\n\nSo, $L = \\frac{1}{394784}$\n$L \\approx 2.533 \\times 10^{-6}$ H\n\nThis is approximately $2.53 \\mu$H.\n\nComparing this with the given options:\nA. 1.00 μH\nB. 1.53 μH\nC. 3.14 μH\nD. 3.53 μH\nE. 0.75 μH\nF. 2.00 μH\nG. 5.00 μH\nH. 4.00 μH\nI. 1.77 μH\nJ. 2.53 μH\n\nThe calculated value is closest to option J.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{J}$.",
