    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10720",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the Laplace transform of f(t) = t^2.\n\nOptions: \nA. (2 / s^4)\nB. (1 / s^3)\nC. (t^2 / s)\nD. (t^2 / s^3)\nE. (2 / s^3)\nF. (4 / s^3)\nG. (3 / s^4)\nH. (2 / s^2)\nI. (3 / s^3)\nJ. (1 / s^2)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Laplace transform of $t^n$ is given by the formula $\\mathcal{L}\\{t^n\\} = \\frac{n!}{s^{n+1}}$, where $n$ is a non-negative integer and $s > 0$. In this problem, we have $f(t) = t^2$, so $n=2$.\n\nUsing the formula, we can calculate the Laplace transform of $f(t)$:\n$\\mathcal{L}\\{t^2\\} = \\frac{2!}{s^{2+1}} = \\frac{2}{s^3}$.\n\nComparing this result with the given options, we find that option E matches our calculated Laplace transform.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{E}$.",
