    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A test charge q C, moving with a velocityv= (i_x +i_y) m/sec, experiences no force in a region of electric and magnetic fields. If the magnetic flux density B= (i_x - 2i_z)Wb/m^2, findE.\n\nOptions: \nA. (i_z - 2i_y) volts/m\nB. (-i_x + i_y) volts/m\nC. (3i_x - i_y - 2i_z) volts/m\nD. (2ix - 2i_y +i_z) volts/m\nE. (i_x - 2i_z) volts/m\nF. (2i_x - i_y) volts/m\nG. (i_x +i_y) volts/m\nH. (2ix + 2i_y -i_z) volts/m\nI. (i_y + i_z) volts/m\nJ. (i_x + 2i_y + i_z) volts/m\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Lorentz force on a test charge q moving with velocity v in electric field E and magnetic field B is given by F = q(E + v x B).\nGiven that the test charge experiences no force, F = 0. Thus, E + v x B = 0, or E = -v x B.\nThe velocity is v = (i_x + i_y) m/sec and the magnetic flux density is B = (i_x - 2i_z) Wb/m^2.\nNow, we calculate the cross product v x B:\nv x B = (i_x + i_y) m/sec x (i_x - 2i_z) Wb/m^2\nv x B = (i_x x i_x) + (i_x x -2i_z) + (i_y x i_x) + (i_y x -2i_z)\nv x B = 0 + (-2(i_x x i_z)) + (i_y x i_x) + (-2(i_y x i_z))\nRecall that i_x x i_x = 0, i_x x i_z = -i_y, i_y x i_x = -i_z, and i_y x i_z = i_x.\nv x B = 0 + (-2(-i_y)) + (-i_z) + (-2(i_x))\nv x B = 2i_y - i_z - 2i_x\nv x B = (-2i_x + 2i_y - i_z) m^2/sec * Wb/m^2 = (-2i_x + 2i_y - i_z) V/m.\nNow, we find E = -v x B:\nE = -(-2i_x + 2i_y - i_z) V/m\nE = (2i_x - 2i_y + i_z) V/m.\n\nComparing this result with the given options, we find that option D matches.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{D}$.",
