    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Anelectrethas a permanent electric dipole moment in the absenceof free charges. Given anelectretsphere of radius R, with electricpolarisationvectorP= r̂ Po r. Determine the bound charge density \\rho', electric displacementvectorD, and the electric fieldEas functions ofr.\n\nOptions: \nA. ρ' = P_0 / 3, D = ε_0r̂P_0, E = r̂(3P_0 / ε_0) for r < R and E(r > R) = r̂(P_0 / ε_0)\nB. ρ' = -P_0 / r^2, D = ε_0r̂P_0r, E = -r̂(P_0 / ε_0r^2) for r < R and E(r > R) = -r̂(P_0 / ε_0R^2)\nC. ρ' = 2P_0, D = ε_0r̂P_0r, E = r̂(2P_0r / ε_0) for r < R and E(r > R) = r̂(2P_0R / ε_0)\nD. \nho' = - 3P_0, D = 0, E = - r̂(P_0r / \\epsilon_0) for r > R and E(r < R) = 0\nE. \nho' = - 3P_0, D = 0, E = - r̂(P_0r / \\epsilon_0) for r < R and E(r > R) = 0\nF. ρ' = 0, D = ε_0r̂P_0, E = r̂(P_0r^2 / ε_0) for r < R and E(r > R) = 0\nG. ρ' = P_0r, D = ε_0r̂(P_0r^2), E = r̂(P_0 / ε_0) for r < R and E(r > R) = r̂(P_0R / ε_0)\nH. ρ' = -2P_0/r, D = ε_0r̂(P_0r), E = -r̂(2P_0 / ε_0r) for r < R and E(r > R) = -r̂(2P_0 / ε_0R)\nI. \nho' = 3P_0, D = 1, E = r̂(P_0r / \\epsilon_0) for r < R and E(r > R) = 0\nJ. \nho' = - 3P_0, D = 1, E = - r̂(P_0r / \\epsilon_0) for r < R and E(r > R) = 1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
