    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10159",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The intensity of solar radiation at a point in space that is at the mean distance of the earth from the sun is 1.35 × 10^3 J \\bullet m^-2 \\bullet sec^-1. If radiation from the sun were all at one wavelength, what would be the amplitude of electromagnetic waves from the sun at the position of the earth?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.01 × 10^3 V \bullet m^-1 and 3.70 × 10^-6Wb\bullet m^-2\nB. 1.00 × 10^3 V \bullet m^-1 and 3.00 × 10^-6Wb\bullet m^-2\nC. 1.01 × 10^3 V \bullet m^-1 and 3.37 × 10^-6Wb\bullet m^-2\nD. 1.11 × 10^3 V \bullet m^-1 and 4.37 × 10^-6Wb\bullet m^-2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The intensity of solar radiation is given by the Poynting vector magnitude, $S = \\frac{1}{2} c \\epsilon_0 E_0^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\frac{c}{\\mu_0} B_0^2$.\nWe are given $S = 1.35 \\times 10^3 J \\cdot m^{-2} \\cdot sec^{-1}$.\nWe can find the amplitude of the electric field, $E_0$, using $S = \\frac{1}{2} c \\epsilon_0 E_0^2$.\nRearranging for $E_0$, we get $E_0 = \\sqrt{\\frac{2S}{c \\epsilon_0}}$.\nUsing $c = 3 \\times 10^8 m/s$ and $\\epsilon_0 = 8.85 \\times 10^{-12} C^2/(N \\cdot m^2)$, we get:\n$E_0 = \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\times 1.35 \\times 10^3}{3 \\times 10^8 \\times 8.85 \\times 10^{-12}}} \\approx \\sqrt{\\frac{2.7 \\times 10^3}{26.55 \\times 10^{-4}}} \\approx \\sqrt{1.0169 \\times 10^6} \\approx 1008.4 V/m$\nThis is approximately $1.01 \\times 10^3 V/m$.\n\nNow we find the amplitude of the magnetic field, $B_0$, using $S = \\frac{1}{2} \\frac{c}{\\mu_0} B_0^2$.\nRearranging for $B_0$, we get $B_0 = \\sqrt{\\frac{2S \\mu_0}{c}}$.\nUsing $\\mu_0 = 4\\pi \\times 10^{-7} Tm/A$:\n$B_0 = \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\times 1.35 \\times 10^3 \\times 4\\pi \\times 10^{-7}}{3 \\times 10^8}} \\approx \\sqrt{\\frac{10.8 \\times 10^{-4} \\times \\pi}{3 \\times 10^8}} \\approx \\sqrt{1.13 \\times 10^{-11}} \\approx 3.36 \\times 10^{-6} T$\nThis is approximately $3.37 \\times 10^{-6} Wb/m^2$.\n\nComparing these values, option C ($1.01 \\times 10^3 V/m$ and $3.37 \\times 10^{-6} Wb/m^2$) matches our calculations.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 301,
        "output_tokens": 637,
        "total_tokens": 938
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
