    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10172",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A mine hoist can lift a maximum load of 5 tons. (a) For the hoist select a 6 × 19 plow steel wire rope and also specify the minimum diameter for the sheave. (b) For the rope and the sheave selected in (a) calculate the number of bends to failure.\n\nOptions: \nA. Rope diameter = 1 in, Sheave diameter = 22 in, Number of bends to failure = 60,000\nB. Rope diameter = 1/2 in, Sheave diameter = 18 in, Number of bends to failure = 30,000\nC. Rope diameter = 7/8 in, Sheave diameter = 21 in, Number of bends to failure = 50,000\nD. Rope diameter = 3/4 in, Sheave diameter = 20 in, Number of bends to failure = 45,000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
