    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10465",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 7-hp motor takes 6.3 kilowatts at full load. What is its efficiency ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 75%\nB. 86%\nC. 95%\nD. 60%\nE. 80%\nF. 83%\nG. 65%\nH. 70%\nI. 78%\nJ. 90%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The problem asks for the efficiency of a motor. Efficiency is defined as the ratio of output power to input power, usually expressed as a percentage.\n\nFirst, we need to convert the output power from horsepower (hp) to kilowatts (kW).\nWe know that 1 hp = 0.746 kW.\nOutput power = 7 hp * 0.746 kW/hp = 5.222 kW.\n\nInput power = 6.3 kW.\n\nEfficiency (%) = (Output power / Input power) * 100%\nEfficiency (%) = (5.222 kW / 6.3 kW) * 100%\nEfficiency (%) = 0.82888... * 100%\nEfficiency (%) = 82.888...%\n\nNow, we compare this calculated efficiency to the given options.\nA. 75%\nB. 86%\nC. 95%\nD. 60%\nE. 80%\nF. 83%\nG. 65%\nH. 70%\nI. 78%\nJ. 90%\n\nThe closest option to 82.888% is 83%.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{F}$",
