  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10601",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Gaseous hydrochloric acid dissociates in water as described bythe following chemical reaction : HCl(g) \\rightarrow H^+(aq) +Cl^-(aq) Using the following heats of formation, calculate \\DeltaH°_77°F for thereaction. Heats of formation @ 77°F HCl-\\DeltaH_f= - 87.54 Btu/mole H^+ -\\DeltaH_f= 0 Btu/mole Cl^- -\\DeltaH_f= - 158.8 Btu/mole\n\nOptions: \nA. 87.54 Btu\nB. -87.54 Btu\nC. 0 Btu\nD. 158.8 Btu\nE. 71.26 Btu\nF. -158.8 Btu\nG. 246.34 Btu\nH. - 71.26 Btu\nI. -246.34 Btu\nJ. -175.34 Btu\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The change in enthalpy for a reaction ($\\Delta H^\\circ_{rxn}$) can be calculated using the heats of formation ($\\Delta H_f^\\circ$) of the products and reactants:\n\n$\\Delta H^\\circ_{rxn} = \\sum (\\text{moles of product} \\times \\Delta H_f^\\circ[\\text{product}]) - \\sum (\\text{moles of reactant} \\times \\Delta H_f^\\circ[\\text{reactant}])$\n\nFor the given reaction, HCl(g) $\\rightarrow$ $H^+$ (aq) + $Cl^-$ (aq):\n\nReactants: 1 mole of HCl(g) with $\\Delta H_f^\\circ = -87.54$ Btu/mole\nProducts: 1 mole of $H^+$ (aq) with $\\Delta H_f^\\circ = 0$ Btu/mole, and 1 mole of $Cl^-$ (aq) with $\\Delta H_f^\\circ = -158.8$ Btu/mole\n\n$\\Delta H^\\circ_{77°F} = [(1 \\times 0) + (1 \\times -158.8)] - [1 \\times -87.54]$\n$\\Delta H^\\circ_{77°F} = [-158.8] - [-87.54]$\n$\\Delta H^\\circ_{77°F} = -158.8 + 87.54$\n$\\Delta H^\\circ_{77°F} = -71.26$ Btu/mole\n\nThe correct answer is H.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{H}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 275,
        "output_tokens": 357,
