  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10076",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Five resistances of 10, 15, 20, 25, and 30 ohms are connected in parallel. Calculate the joint resistance.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3.46 ohms\nB. 4.56 ohms\nC. 8.23 ohms\nD. 4.12 ohms\nE. 6.78 ohms\nF. 7.89 ohms\nG. 1.92 ohms\nH. 2.34 ohms\nI. 2.21 ohms\nJ. 5.67 ohms\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The formula for the equivalent resistance ($R_{eq}$) of resistors connected in parallel is:\n$\\frac{1}{R_{eq}} = \\frac{1}{R_1} + \\frac{1}{R_2} + \\frac{1}{R_3} + \\frac{1}{R_4} + \\frac{1}{R_5}$\n\nGiven the resistances are 10, 15, 20, 25, and 30 ohms.\n$\\frac{1}{R_{eq}} = \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{20} + \\frac{1}{25} + \\frac{1}{30}$\nTo add these fractions, we find a common denominator, which is 300.\n$\\frac{1}{R_{eq}} = \\frac{30}{300} + \\frac{20}{300} + \\frac{15}{300} + \\frac{12}{300} + \\frac{10}{300}$\n$\\frac{1}{R_{eq}} = \\frac{30 + 20 + 15 + 12 + 10}{300}$\n$\\frac{1}{R_{eq}} = \\frac{87}{300}$\nNow, we find the equivalent resistance by taking the reciprocal:\n$R_{eq} = \\frac{300}{87}$\n$R_{eq} \\approx 3.448$ ohms\n\nComparing this value with the given options, option A is the closest.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{A}$.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 186,
        "output_tokens": 373,
        "total_tokens": 559
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
