    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The woman has a single gene deletion, meaning she is a carrier for a single α-thalassemia mutation. The man has a two-gene deletion, and since it's in trans, it means one of his parents contributed one deletion and the other parent contributed the other deletion, making him affected with a more severe form of α-thalassemia. Therefore, the woman's genotype can be represented as -α/-α (one deletion on each chromosome), and the man's genotype can be represented as --/αα (two gene deletion on one chromosome and two normal genes on the other). Their offspring will inherit one alpha-globin gene cluster from each parent. There is a 50% chance that an offspring will inherit the single gene deletion from the mother and a 50% chance of inheriting the two-gene deletion from the father. Thus, there is a 50% chance of inheriting the two-gene deletion.\n\nThe correct answer is B.",
