      "generated_answer": "To calculate the relative risk (RR), we first determine the incidence of cancer death in both groups. Among those who took Drug X, the probability of death from cancer is \\( \\frac{100}{200} = 0.5 \\), and among those who did not take Drug X, it is \\( \\frac{100}{400} = 0.25 \\). Therefore, the relative risk is \\( \\frac{0.5}{0.25} = 2 \\), indicating that individuals who take Drug X have two times the risk of dying from this type of cancer.\n\nThe correct choice is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).",
