    "global index": "MMLUPro_health_5484",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All of the following are true regarding the function of neurons EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. The refractory period prevents the neuron from initiating a new action potential.\nB. The transmitting neuron secretes neurotransmitters into the synaptic cleft from its dendrites.\nC. An action potential is initiated when the axon hillock reaches the threshold potential.\nD. The action potential travels along the axon away from the cell body.\nE. Hyperpolarization occurs when the membrane potential becomes more negative than the resting potential.\nF. The flow of sodium into the neuron depolarizes the membrane in the first phase of an action potential.\nG. Hyperpolarization at the end of an action potential is one mechanism by which neurons limit the rate at which action potentials may fire.\nH. The neuron releases neurotransmitters into the synaptic cleft from the axon terminals.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The question asks for the statement that is NOT true regarding the function of neurons. Let's evaluate each option:\n\nA. The refractory period indeed prevents the neuron from initiating a new action potential immediately after firing. This is true.\nB. Neurotransmitters are secreted from the axon terminals, not the dendrites, of the transmitting neuron. This statement is false.\nC. An action potential is initiated at the axon hillock when the membrane potential reaches the threshold potential. This is true.\nD. The action potential propagates along the axon, moving away from the cell body towards the axon terminals. This is true.\nE. Hyperpolarization means the membrane potential becomes more negative than the resting potential, making it harder to fire an action potential. This is true.\nF. The influx of sodium ions causes depolarization, which is the first phase of an action potential. This is true.\nG. Hyperpolarization does contribute to limiting the firing rate of neurons by making it take longer to reach the threshold potential again. This is true.\nH. Neurotransmitters are released from the axon terminals into the synaptic cleft to transmit signals to the next neuron. This is true.\n\nBased on this analysis, option B is the incorrect statement.\n\nThe transmitting neuron secretes neurotransmitters into the synaptic cleft from its axon terminals, not its dendrites. Dendrites are responsible for receiving signals.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{B}$.",
