    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The interaction between broad-spectrum antibiotics and coumarin anticoagulants is a well-documented phenomenon. Broad-spectrum antibiotics can alter the gut flora, which are responsible for synthesizing a significant portion of vitamin K. Vitamin K is essential for the synthesis of clotting factors, and a reduction in its availability will lead to a decreased ability of the blood to clot. This, in turn, enhances the anticoagulant effect of coumarin drugs like warfarin.\n\nTherefore, the most likely correct answer is:\n\nC. Increased because of reduction of vitamin 'K' sources\n\nThe explanation is that antibiotics disrupt the gut bacteria that produce vitamin K. A decrease in vitamin K leads to reduced synthesis of clotting factors, thus potentiating the anticoagulant effect of coumarin drugs.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$.",
