    "global index": "MedMCQA_2003",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Calculate net filtration pressure with the following data: PGC = 42 mm Hg pGC = 12 mm Hg PBC= 16 mm Hg Assume that no proteins were filtered.\n\nOptions: \nA. 34 mm Hg\nB. Data not sufficient\nC. 14 mm Hg\nD. 28 mm Hg\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-2.5-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is **C**.\n\nHere's why:\n\nNet filtration pressure (NFP) is calculated using the formula: NFP = (PGC + πBC) - (PBC + πGC).\nIn this case:\n* PGC (glomerular capillary hydrostatic pressure) = 42 mm Hg\n* πGC (glomerular capillary oncotic pressure) = 12 mm Hg\n* PBC (Bowman's capsule hydrostatic pressure) = 16 mm Hg\n* πBC (Bowman's capsule oncotic pressure) = 0 mm Hg (since no proteins were filtered)\n\nNFP = (42 + 0) - (16 + 12)\nNFP = 42 - 28\nNFP = 14 mm Hg\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{C}$",
      "success": true,
