      "generated_answer": "To calculate the standard error (SE) of the mean, you can use the formula: SE = SD / √n, where SD is the standard deviation and n is the sample size. Here, the SD is 1 and n is 100, so SE = 1 / √100 = 1 / 10 = 0.1. Thus, the correct answer is \\boxed{B}.",
